YO, FOR REAL?

230
00:10:06,774 --> 00:10:08,976
YEAH, YEAH, I GOT YOU.

231
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:13,013
THIRSTY?

232
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,247
GIRL, I WORKED
A DOUBLE SHIFT

233
00:10:14,314 --> 00:10:15,749
AT THE RESTAURANT
TO GET THIS NIGHT OFF.

234
00:10:15,816 --> 00:10:18,385
I'M ABOUT TO HAVE A BALL.
YOU SHOULD, TOO.

235
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:21,554
I'M HAVING FUN.

236
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,190
OH, STOP!

237
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:25,158
[BOTH GIGGLE]

238
00:10:25,225 --> 00:10:27,594
SEE? SEE, THIS IS
WHY I DON'T DATE.

239
00:10:27,661 --> 00:10:28,696
ONLY GUYS I MEET ARE
IN THE INDUSTRY,

240
00:10:28,762 --> 00:10:31,031
AND THEY AIN'T NEVER GOT
THEIR SHIT TOGETHER.

241
00:10:34,167 --> 00:10:36,804
WHAT, LIKE HIM?

242
00:10:41,341 --> 00:10:42,642
Sidney, voice over: EVER
THOUGHT YOU'D SEE THE DAY

243
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:44,044
HIP-HOP GREW UP?

244
00:10:44,111 --> 00:10:47,547
FROM RED KOOL-AID BLOCK
PARTIES IN THE BRONX

245
00:10:47,614 --> 00:10:49,750
TO CHAMPAGNE TOASTS
IN SOHO.

246
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:55,322
OOH! HA HA HA!

247
00:11:00,193 --> 00:11:02,662
WHAT'RE YOU
DRINKING, BEAUTIFUL?

248
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:04,397
UH, UM...

249
00:11:04,464 --> 00:11:06,066
THAT'LL BE A PERFECT 10

250
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:08,335
FOR THE LADY,
IF YOU PLEASE.

251
00:11:08,401 --> 00:11:09,903
AND A KETEL ONE
MARTINI

252
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:11,271
UP WITH A TWIST
FOR THE GENTLEMAN.

253
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:14,274
GET UP OFF THAT CHAIR
AND HUG ME, GIRL.

254
00:11:14,341 --> 00:11:16,509
WHAT'S UP, BABY?

255
00:11:16,576 --> 00:11:18,478
I HAVE MISSED YOU
SO MUCH.

256
00:11:18,545 --> 00:11:20,613
I MISSED YOU, TOO.
HOW YOU BEEN?

257
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,082
KISS IT.

258
00:11:22,149 --> 00:11:23,050
LOOK AT YOU.

259
00:11:23,116 --> 00:11:27,387
THERE YOU ARE.
OH, MY GOD.

260
00:11:27,454 --> 00:11:29,056
I GOT YOU, I GOT YOU.

261
00:11:29,122 --> 00:11:30,623
DRE, STOP IT! I CAN'T
BELIEVE YOU LEFT ME

262
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,691
OVER THERE
WITH THAT MAN.

263
00:11:31,759 --> 00:11:33,493
DON'T BE MAD.
KISS ME, KISS ME.

264
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,627
GIMME A KISS,
GIMME A KISS.

265
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:36,163
YES, THAT'S
WHAT I LIKE.

266
00:11:36,229 --> 00:11:37,697
SIDNEY HERE IS SOMEBODY
I WANT YOU TO MEET.

267
00:11:37,765 --> 00:11:38,799
OH, MY GOD!

268
00:11:38,866 --> 00:11:40,500
SIDNEY, REESE.

269
00:11:40,567 --> 00:11:42,202
IT'S SO GOOD
TO MEET YOU.

270
00:11:42,269 --> 00:11:45,138
OH, MY GOD! I'VE HEARD
SO MUCH ABOUT YOU.

271
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:47,007
OH, WELL, I HOPE
IT WASN'T TOO BAD.

272
00:11:47,074 --> 00:11:48,909
NO, AND YOU LOOK GREAT.

273
00:11:48,976 --> 00:11:50,744
BUT I CAN'T COMPETE WITH
YOU IN THAT DRESS.

274
00:11:50,811 --> 00:11:52,880
OH, PLEASE, I THINK YOU
ARE WEARING THAT DRESS.

275
00:11:52,946 --> 00:11:54,815
AND YOUR EARRINGS
ARE SO BEAUTIFUL.

276
00:11:54,882 --> 00:11:56,649
[CLEARS THROAT]

277
00:11:56,716 --> 00:11:59,119
DO YOU HEAR
SOMETHING, SIDNEY?

278
00:11:59,186 --> 00:12:00,653
YEAH, SOUNDED
LIKE A MALE EGO.

279
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,722
HA HA HA HA!

280
00:12:02,790 --> 00:12:03,991
THAT'S REAL FUNNY.

281
00:12:05,125 --> 00:12:06,593
ANYWAY, THIS IS CUTE.
Y'ALL SHOULD TAKE

282
00:12:06,659 --> 00:12:08,361
THIS LITTLE ACT
ON THE ROAD.

283
00:12:08,428 --> 00:12:10,063
WE'RE JUST
TEASING YOU.

284
00:12:10,130 --> 00:12:11,999
OH, THERE'S STEVE.
I GOTTA TALK TO HIM

285
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:14,434
ABOUT THE ARISTA
DEAL. SIDNEY...

286
00:12:14,501 --> 00:12:15,535
GOOD TO MEET YOU.

287
00:12:15,602 --> 00:12:16,636
OK.

288
00:12:16,703 --> 00:12:17,771
HURRY UP. I LOVE YOU.

289
00:12:17,838 --> 00:12:19,506
I LOVE YOU.

290
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:20,607
NOT BAD, NOT BAD.

291
00:12:20,673 --> 00:12:22,943
MM-HMM.

292
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:25,012
YEAH, SHE'S PRETTY
MUCH AMAZING.

293
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:26,013
AMAZING?

294
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,214
MM-HMM.

295
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,515
THAT'S NOT A WORD
I'VE HEARD YOU USE

296
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:29,783
TO DESCRIBE
ONE OF YOUR WOMEN.

297
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:31,751
OH, SHE AIN'T LIKE
ANY OF THE OTHERS.

298
00:12:31,819 --> 00:12:33,520
FOR REAL.

299
00:12:38,491 --> 00:12:39,759
WHAT'S UP?

300
00:12:39,827 --> 00:12:41,194
I WANT TO SHOW YOU
SOMETHING.

301
00:12:45,532 --> 00:12:46,599
IS THAT
WHAT I THINK IT IS?

302
00:12:46,666 --> 00:12:48,235
YEAH.

303
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:52,539
THINK I'M GONNA
DO IT TONIGHT, SID.

304
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,374
WHAT?
UH-HUH.

305
00:12:54,441 --> 00:12:56,576
ARE YOU SERIOUS?
YEAH.

306
00:12:56,643 --> 00:12:59,279
BUT, DRE,
YOU'VE KNOWN HER

307
00:12:59,346 --> 00:13:00,547
FOR LIKE
5 MINUTES.

308
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:02,715
I KNOW, I KNOW, BUT, UM...

309
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:05,986
I--I THINK SHE'S THE ONE.
SO I'M RETIRING

310
00:13:06,053 --> 00:13:07,888
THE "SLOW JAMS DELUXE
GET THE DRAWERS" TAPE.

311
00:13:07,955 --> 00:13:10,590
THE "SLOW JAMS DELUXE
GET THE DRAWERS" TAPE?

312
00:13:10,657 --> 00:13:13,193
YEAH. THE ONE WITH
LUTHER, SADE,

313
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:15,829
AND THE EXTENDED MIX
OF PRINCE'S ADORE, SO...

314
00:13:15,896 --> 00:13:17,364
DAMN, IT'S LIKE THAT?

315
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:19,266
I'M FOR REAL.

316
00:13:21,334 --> 00:13:23,470
WHAT, WHY ARE YOU
LOOKING AT ME LIKE THAT?

317
00:13:23,536 --> 00:13:25,638
I DON'T KNOW.
WE'RE--

318
00:13:25,705 --> 00:13:27,107
WE'RE GROWN-UPS.

319
00:13:27,174 --> 00:13:28,575
I'M SO GLAD YOU'RE HERE.

320
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:31,912
OH, I'M HAPPY
TO BE HERE. OHH!

321
00:13:31,979 --> 00:13:34,514
ALL RIGHT,
I'M ABOUT TO GO IN.

322
00:13:34,581 --> 00:13:35,682
YOU'LL BE FINE.

323
00:13:35,748 --> 00:13:37,750
YOU'LL BE FINE.
TRUST YOURSELF.

324
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:39,319
ALL RIGHT.
MY BREATH TART?

325
00:13:39,386 --> 00:13:41,054
NO, YOU'RE COOL.

326
00:13:41,121 --> 00:13:43,123
ALL RIGHT. HERE WE GO.

327
00:13:58,738 --> 00:14:01,308
[MUFFLED] OHH!
OH, MY GOD!

328
00:14:01,374 --> 00:14:03,410
DRE, OH, MY GOD!

329
00:14:03,476 --> 00:14:06,379
YES, YES, YES!

330
00:14:08,148 --> 00:14:11,051
* WAS IT GOOD ENOUGH
FOR YOU? *

331
00:14:11,118 --> 00:14:12,319
GIRL,
I CAN'T BELIEVE

332
00:14:12,385 --> 00:14:13,586
YOU'VE BEEN HERE
DAMN NEAR A MONTH

333
00:14:13,653 --> 00:14:15,022
AND YOU STILL
NOT UNPACKED.

334
00:14:15,088 --> 00:14:17,024
I'VE BEEN BUSY.

335
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:18,091
I MEAN, THERE'S THIS
LITTLE JOB I HAVE

336
00:14:18,158 --> 00:14:19,359
AT THIS LITTLE
MAGAZINE.

337
00:14:19,426 --> 00:14:23,263
BESIDES, THERE'S ORDER
IN THIS CHAOS.

338
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:26,299
I KNOW WHERE EVERYTHING IS
AND WHERE EVERYTHING GOES.

339
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:30,170
SO, UH, WHERE DOES
THIS GO? OOH!

340
00:14:30,237 --> 00:14:32,205
IT'S NOT WHAT YOU THINK.

341
00:14:32,272 --> 00:14:33,806
IT'S A MASSAGER
FROM BROOKSTONE.

342
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,742
OH, COME ON, SID,
LIKE I DON'T KNOW--

343
00:14:35,808 --> 00:14:37,044
IT'S A MASSAGER!

344
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:38,878
MEN TAKE TOO MUCH
OF YOUR TIME.

345
00:14:38,946 --> 00:14:41,448
TIME I DON'T HAVE.

346
00:14:41,514 --> 00:14:43,550
YOU'RE TURNING INTO
A TERRY McMILLIAN CHARACTER.

347
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:45,852
DON'T SAY THAT,
THAT'S COLD!

348
00:14:45,919 --> 00:14:47,120
I'M TELLING YOU
YOU'RE IN TROUBLE.

349
00:14:47,187 --> 00:14:49,056
OH, IT'S JUST I NEVER
SEEM TO FIND ANYONE

350
00:14:49,122 --> 00:14:50,657
ON THE SAME PAGE
WITH ME.

351
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:51,925
WHAT, LIKE DRE?

352
00:14:51,992 --> 00:14:53,226
OH, HERE WE GO.

353
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:54,294
COME ON.
YOU'RE GONNA TELL ME

354
00:14:54,361 --> 00:14:56,029
YOU NEVER THOUGHT
ABOUT HOOKING UP?

355
00:14:56,096 --> 00:15:00,333
DRE ASKED ME ONCE
WHEN I WAS AT COLUMBIA

356
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,469
IF WE SHOULD TRY BEING
MORE THAN JUST FRIENDS,

357
00:15:02,535 --> 00:15:06,039
AND...I TOLD HIM NO.

358
00:15:06,106 --> 00:15:09,542
NO?! WHAT IS WRONG
WITH YOU, GIRL?

359
00:15:09,609 --> 00:15:11,811
I MEAN, WE'VE BEEN THROUGH
EVERYTHING TOGETHER.

360
00:15:11,878 --> 00:15:13,413
EXACTLY. SO IF
YOU TWO HOOK UP,

361
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,315
YOU GET THE BEST
OF BOTH WORLDS.

362
00:15:15,382 --> 00:15:18,418
YOU GET THE BUDDY
AND THE BOOTY.

363
00:15:18,485 --> 00:15:20,753
I HEAR YOU,
BUT RELATIONSHIPS BREAK UP.

364
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:21,921
PEOPLE GET ANGRY,

365
00:15:21,989 --> 00:15:24,057
THEY NEVER WANT TO
TALK TO EACH OTHER AGAIN.

366
00:15:24,124 --> 00:15:25,592
I MEAN, YOU'RE DIVORCED.
TERRELL WAS YOUR ACE, RIGHT?

367
00:15:25,658 --> 00:15:26,826
YOU STILL TALK TO HIM?

368
00:15:26,893 --> 00:15:28,528
ME AND TERRELL TALK
ALL THE TIME.

369
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:29,762
WE TALK
ABOUT ALIMONY,

370
00:15:29,829 --> 00:15:31,631
WE TALK ABOUT
THAT TRAMP...

371
00:15:31,698 --> 00:15:33,900
EXACTLY, EXACTLY.

372
00:15:33,967 --> 00:15:35,102
AND YOU KNOW DRE.

373
00:15:35,168 --> 00:15:36,803
HE'S NEVER BEEN WITH A WOMAN
MORE THAN A MONTH.

374
00:15:36,869 --> 00:15:37,837
YEAH, WELL,
LOOKS LIKE

375
00:15:37,904 --> 00:15:39,206
HE'S GONNA
KEEP THIS ONE.

376
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:41,441
GUESS SO. OOH,
SHE INVITED ME

377
00:15:41,508 --> 00:15:42,976
TO HER BRIDAL TEA
SHOWER THINGY,

378
00:15:43,043 --> 00:15:44,344
AND I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO BRING.

379
00:15:44,411 --> 00:15:46,246
YOU HAVEN'T
CHANGED A BIT.

380
00:15:46,313 --> 00:15:47,247
WANT ME TO PICK
SOMETHING UP FOR YOU?

381
00:15:47,314 --> 00:15:48,881
OH, WOULD YOU,
WOULD YOU?

382
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,283
I GOT YOU, CUZ,
I GOT YOU COVERED.

383
00:15:50,350 --> 00:15:52,285
YOU'RE THE BEST
COUSIN IN THE WORLD.

384
00:15:52,352 --> 00:15:53,953
SO WHAT DO YOU WANT ME
TO DO WITH YOUR MASSAGER?

385
00:15:54,021 --> 00:15:56,689
HIGH SPEED, LOW.

386
00:15:56,756 --> 00:15:58,558
[BOTH LAUGHING]

387
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,970
Reese: SIDNEY!

388
00:16:11,038 --> 00:16:13,606
YOU MADE IT! HI!

389
00:16:13,673 --> 00:16:15,775
HEY.

390
00:16:15,842 --> 00:16:17,810
OH, THANK YOU.

391
00:16:17,877 --> 00:16:21,248
I WONDER WHAT THIS IS.

392
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:24,551
Woman: AND WE CALLED
HER REESE'S PIECES.

393
00:16:24,617 --> 00:16:27,020
Second Woman: OK,
LET'S MOVE ON TO THE GROOM.

394
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:29,156
I'LL ASK
THE SAME QUESTIONS.

395
00:16:29,222 --> 00:16:32,692
WHAT IS DRE'S MIDDLE NAME?

396
00:16:32,759 --> 00:16:34,027
FINE.

397
00:16:34,094 --> 00:16:35,162
ROMULUS.

398
00:16:35,228 --> 00:16:36,196
WHAT'D YOU SAY,
SIDNEY?

399
00:16:36,263 --> 00:16:38,131
YOU KNOW THE ANSWER?

400
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:40,133
ROMULUS.

401
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,268
THAT'S RIGHT.

402
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:43,136
THAT'S THE NAME OF
THIS SHAKE DANCER,

403
00:16:43,203 --> 00:16:44,604
WORKS CLUB
MOZAMBIQUE.

404
00:16:44,671 --> 00:16:45,972
OK, AUNT BETTY.

405
00:16:46,039 --> 00:16:47,574
OK, ANYWAY...

406
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,441
ROMULUS IS RIGHT.

407
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:51,744
WHAT IS DRE'S
FAVORITE DRINK?

408
00:16:51,811 --> 00:16:53,513
COSMO.
A POLAR BEAR.

409
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,482
KETEL ONE MARTINI
UP WITH A TWIST,

410
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:58,218
BUT IF HE'S TRYING
TO SHOW OFF, MACALLAN 25.

411
00:16:58,285 --> 00:17:02,122
RIGHT AGAIN.
MACALLAN 25.

412
00:17:02,189 --> 00:17:03,323
ALL RIGHT, THEN.

413
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:07,260
WHAT IS DRE'S
FAVORITE SONG?

414
00:17:07,327 --> 00:17:09,896
THE BRIDGE IS OVER,
BOOGIE DOWN PRODUCTIONS.

415
00:17:09,962 --> 00:17:12,632
OK, SID CAN'T
PLAY ANYMORE.

416
00:17:12,699 --> 00:17:14,301
SHE KNOWS TOO MUCH.

417
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:16,803
Reese: OK, LET'S MOVE ON
TO SOMETHING ELSE.

418
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:18,105
HOW ABOUT...

419
00:17:18,171 --> 00:17:20,140
THIS IS FROM MOI.

420
00:17:26,313 --> 00:17:27,980
OH, YOU GUYS,
YOU GUYS!

421
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,716
OOH!
OHH!

422
00:17:29,782 --> 00:17:31,651
HONEYMOON NIGHT ONLY.

423
00:17:31,718 --> 00:17:35,922
YOU'RE SO INCREDIBLE.
I LOVE YOU SO MUCH.

424
00:17:35,988 --> 00:17:37,590
I'M GLAD
YOU LIKE THEM, DARLING.

425
00:17:37,657 --> 00:17:40,927
OK, NEXT, LET'S DO...

426
00:17:40,993 --> 00:17:42,795
SIDNEY'S GIFT.

427
00:17:47,834 --> 00:17:51,604
THANK YOU.
SUCH A SWEETHEART.

428
00:18:03,283 --> 00:18:07,654
NICE. VERY NICE.

429
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,089
THEY'RE GONNA BE
PERFECT WITH MY WHIP.

430
00:18:10,157 --> 00:18:13,293
[WOMEN LAUGHING]

431
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:15,162
Sidney:
I'M GONNA KILL FRANCE!

432
00:18:15,228 --> 00:18:18,030
I WAS
SO EMBARRASSED, DRE.

433
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:19,666
AND HUNGRY.

434
00:18:19,732 --> 00:18:20,600
I BET YOU WERE.

435
00:18:20,667 --> 00:18:21,901
I MEAN, THEY DIDN'T
HAVE ANYTHING

436
00:18:21,968 --> 00:18:23,170
BUT THOSE LITTLE
CUCUMBER SANDWICHES

437
00:18:23,236 --> 00:18:24,137
WITH THE CRUST CUT OFF.

438
00:18:24,204 --> 00:18:25,905
JUST KEEP
THE CHANGE.

439
00:18:25,972 --> 00:18:27,073
THANKS FOR MEETING ME.

440
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:29,142
YOU'RE MY DAWG.

441
00:18:31,878 --> 00:18:33,613
[GIGGLES]
IT'S GOOD, HUH?

442
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,582
MMM!

443
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:40,153
I LOVE
THESE BAD BOYS.

444
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:42,822
IT'S TRUE.
I CAN'T EVEN FRONT.

445
00:18:42,889 --> 00:18:44,257
WHENEVER I GO OUT
WITH REESE,

446
00:18:44,324 --> 00:18:46,058
WE ALWAYS GOING
TO SOME FANCY SPOT

447
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,260
WITH WHITE
TABLECLOTHS

448
00:18:47,327 --> 00:18:49,829
AND A LOT
OF SILVERWARE,

449
00:18:49,896 --> 00:18:52,365
HOSTING ONE OF
REESE'S CLIENTS.

450
00:18:52,432 --> 00:18:53,966
I HAVEN'T HAD ONE OF
THESE BAD BOYS

451
00:18:54,033 --> 00:18:55,902
SINCE WE STARTED
DATING.

452
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:57,704
WOW. SHE MUST REALLY
BE SOMETHING.

453
00:18:57,770 --> 00:18:59,839
MMHH.

454
00:18:59,906 --> 00:19:01,308
YEAH, FOR SURE.

455
00:19:01,374 --> 00:19:03,810
SHE'S BROWN SUGAR.

456
00:19:03,876 --> 00:19:04,877
OH, YEAH,
THE BROWN SUGAR.

457
00:19:04,944 --> 00:19:06,078
YEAH.

458
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,415
BREAK IT DOWN FOR ME.

459
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:10,883
YOU KNOW, WE ALL LOOKING
FOR WIFEY MATERIAL.

460
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:12,352
A WOMAN THAT'S FINE,

461
00:19:12,419 --> 00:19:14,521
SMART, CLASSY,
BUT NOT A SNOB.

462
00:19:14,587 --> 00:19:18,024
YOU KNOW, HELLA--HELLA
SEXY, BUT NOT A HO.

463
00:19:18,090 --> 00:19:21,894
THAT'S BROWN SUGAR.
THAT'S MY REESEY.

464
00:19:21,961 --> 00:19:24,297
I MEAN,
DON'T GET CONFUSED

465
00:19:24,364 --> 00:19:26,065
BY HER BUSINESS SUIT.

466
00:19:26,132 --> 00:19:28,134
SHE IS A FREAK
IN THE BEDROOM...

467
00:19:28,201 --> 00:19:29,969
A LITTLE BIT
TOO MUCH INFORMATION.

468
00:19:30,036 --> 00:19:31,638
