00:46:24,649 --> 00:46:26,051
YEAH, MAN.

1172
00:46:26,117 --> 00:46:28,053
SEE, THAT'S WHY I WRITE
AND DON'T RAP.

1173
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:29,587
[LAUGHS]
FOR REAL.

1174
00:46:29,654 --> 00:46:32,057
THAT SONG
REMINDED ME OF US.

1175
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:33,424
IT DOES?

1176
00:46:33,491 --> 00:46:35,126
YEAH,
BACK IN THE DAY.

1177
00:46:35,193 --> 00:46:36,294
DO YOU REMEMBER
THAT FEELING?

1178
00:46:36,361 --> 00:46:38,964
JUST HOW HIP-HOP USED
TO MAKE YOU FEEL?

1179
00:46:39,030 --> 00:46:40,531
ESPECIALLY
BACK THEN.

1180
00:46:40,598 --> 00:46:42,633
IT WAS SO REAL.
IT WAS LIKE AIR.

1181
00:46:42,700 --> 00:46:43,701
DO YOU REMEMBER
HOW YOU FELT

1182
00:46:43,768 --> 00:46:44,769
THE FIRST TIME
YOU HEARD

1183
00:46:44,836 --> 00:46:46,437
THE BRIDGE IS OVER?

1184
00:46:46,504 --> 00:46:47,538
THE FIRST TIME?

1185
00:46:47,605 --> 00:46:48,907
YUP.

1186
00:46:48,974 --> 00:46:50,075
THAT WAS REAL.

1187
00:46:50,141 --> 00:46:52,110
OOH, OR, UM...
YOU GOTS TO CHILL.

1188
00:46:52,177 --> 00:46:54,379
THE SOPHOMORE SKATE PARTY?

1189
00:46:57,382 --> 00:46:59,484
BONITA APPLEBUM.
THAT WAS A TIGHT ONE.

1190
00:46:59,550 --> 00:47:00,518
MM-MMM.

1191
00:47:00,585 --> 00:47:03,121
AND PAUL REVERE.
OOH, I USED TO LOVED THAT.

1192
00:47:03,188 --> 00:47:05,323
SEE, NOW THAT BEAT
WAS TIGHT.

1193
00:47:05,390 --> 00:47:06,191
THE BEASTIE BOYS.

1194
00:47:06,257 --> 00:47:08,159
YEAH, MAN,
THEY CAME WITH IT.

1195
00:47:08,226 --> 00:47:09,294
MM-HMM.

1196
00:47:09,360 --> 00:47:11,629
YOU KNOW...

1197
00:47:11,696 --> 00:47:14,132
I DON'T HAVE
THAT FEELING NO MORE.

1198
00:47:14,199 --> 00:47:15,833
YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M SAYING?

1199
00:47:18,403 --> 00:47:19,637
I CANNOT REMEMBER
THE LAST TIME

1200
00:47:19,704 --> 00:47:22,040
I HAD THAT FEELING.

1201
00:47:22,107 --> 00:47:24,442
I CAN'T--
I CAN'T--

1202
00:47:24,509 --> 00:47:27,278
YOU READY TO TALK?
WHAT'S ON YOUR MIND?

1203
00:47:34,119 --> 00:47:36,521
I QUIT TODAY, SID.

1204
00:47:38,389 --> 00:47:40,791
I LEFT MILLENNIUM.

1205
00:47:40,858 --> 00:47:47,698
I JUST WALKED AWAY
FROM IT ALL TODAY.

1206
00:47:47,765 --> 00:47:50,035
SO, WHATCHA
GONNA DO NOW?

1207
00:47:53,871 --> 00:47:56,341
I'M THINKING...

1208
00:47:56,407 --> 00:47:58,643
I'M THINKING I COULD
START MY OWN LABEL.

1209
00:47:58,709 --> 00:48:01,246
YOU KNOW? YEAH.

1210
00:48:01,312 --> 00:48:03,381
UM, YOU KNOW,
MAKE MUSIC

1211
00:48:03,448 --> 00:48:04,916
THAT I WANT TO MAKE.

1212
00:48:04,983 --> 00:48:06,884
MUSIC THAT I THINK
SHOULD BE OUT THERE.

1213
00:48:06,952 --> 00:48:07,885
YOU KNOW
WHAT I MEAN?

1214
00:48:07,953 --> 00:48:08,920
BRING ON ARTISTS

1215
00:48:08,987 --> 00:48:11,589
AND TREAT 'EM
LIKE PARTNERS.

1216
00:48:11,656 --> 00:48:14,359
MAKE MY MONEY
THE RIGHT WAY.

1217
00:48:14,425 --> 00:48:16,161
SHOOT.

1218
00:48:16,227 --> 00:48:19,397
BE ONE OF THE GOOD
GUYS FOR A CHANGE.

1219
00:48:20,765 --> 00:48:22,367
YOU THINK I'M CRAZY?

1220
00:48:23,768 --> 00:48:24,970
I THINK YOU'RE THE BOMB.

1221
00:48:25,036 --> 00:48:27,205
FOR REAL?

1222
00:48:27,272 --> 00:48:28,406
I THINK
YOU'RE THE BOMB.

1223
00:48:28,473 --> 00:48:30,541
FOR REAL-REAL?
YES.

1224
00:48:30,608 --> 00:48:33,945
DAMN.
THAT'S GREAT, DRE.

1225
00:48:34,012 --> 00:48:35,446
I CAN ALREADY SEE US
AT THE GRAMMYS,

1226
00:48:35,513 --> 00:48:37,815
BASKING IN YOUR SUCCESS.

1227
00:48:37,882 --> 00:48:39,784
OH, I LIKE
HOW THAT SOUNDS.

1228
00:48:39,850 --> 00:48:41,586
THE GRAMMYS.

1229
00:48:41,652 --> 00:48:44,990
DAMN, DRE,
THAT'S GREAT.

1230
00:48:45,056 --> 00:48:48,393
I'M SCARED, SID.

1231
00:48:48,459 --> 00:48:51,829
SO, HOW--
HOW ARE YOU GOING TO--

1232
00:48:51,896 --> 00:48:53,831
YOU GOT THE MONEY?

1233
00:48:53,898 --> 00:48:56,201
UH, I MEAN, I GOT
A LITTLE SOMETHING--

1234
00:48:56,267 --> 00:48:58,236
A LITTLE
SOMETHING SAVED.

1235
00:48:58,303 --> 00:49:01,406
I'M GONNA HAVE TO HIT UP
OTHER SOURCES, BUT...

1236
00:49:01,472 --> 00:49:03,674
YOU KNOW, I AIN'T GONNA
REALLY STRESS ABOUT THAT.

1237
00:49:03,741 --> 00:49:05,943
THAT'S THE LAST THING

1238
00:49:06,011 --> 00:49:07,512
I NEED TO BE
WORRYING ABOUT NOW.

1239
00:49:07,578 --> 00:49:10,615
I'M GONNA START OUT
WITH ONE ARTIST--

1240
00:49:10,681 --> 00:49:13,118
WHAT YOU DOING?

1241
00:49:13,184 --> 00:49:14,552
YOU JUST FOUND
ANOTHER SOURCE.

1242
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:18,389
SID, STOP PLAYING.
I AIN'T--

1243
00:49:18,456 --> 00:49:19,324
TAKE IT.

1244
00:49:19,390 --> 00:49:21,359
NO, I'M NOT TAKING
THAT MONEY FROM YOU.

1245
00:49:21,426 --> 00:49:22,793
COME ON.

1246
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:25,196
LOOK, YOU ARE
MY BEST FRIEND.

1247
00:49:25,263 --> 00:49:26,597
THERE'S NOBODY
THAT BELIEVES IN YOU

1248
00:49:26,664 --> 00:49:28,933
MORE THAN ME.
SO YOU'RE TAKING THIS CHECK,

1249
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:30,935
YOU'RE STARTING
THAT LABEL

1250
00:49:31,002 --> 00:49:33,104
AND IT'S GONNA BE HOT.

1251
00:49:36,674 --> 00:49:39,510
[CHURCH BELL CHIMING]

1252
00:49:41,646 --> 00:49:44,415
ALL RIGHT, GIRL.

1253
00:49:44,482 --> 00:49:45,950
[SIGHS]

1254
00:49:46,017 --> 00:49:47,085
OW!

1255
00:49:47,152 --> 00:49:50,921
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU
SOMETIMES.

1256
00:49:50,988 --> 00:49:53,724
WHOO! SO WHAT YOU
DOING TONIGHT?

1257
00:49:53,791 --> 00:49:55,126
WE GONNA CELEBRATE
OR WHAT?

1258
00:49:55,193 --> 00:49:58,029
I CAN'T, I HAVE--
I HAVE A DATE.

1259
00:50:00,631 --> 00:50:03,634
OH, WITH KELBY?
YEAH.

1260
00:50:03,701 --> 00:50:05,270
SO YOU SAID
YES, HUH?

1261
00:50:05,336 --> 00:50:06,871
WHAT'S
THIS CAT'S NUMBER

1262
00:50:06,937 --> 00:50:07,838
'CAUSE I'M GONNA
CALL HIM UP

1263
00:50:07,905 --> 00:50:08,906
AND CANCEL FOR YOU

1264
00:50:08,973 --> 00:50:10,208
'CAUSE YOU HANGING
WITH ME TONIGHT.

1265
00:50:10,275 --> 00:50:11,442
UH-UH.
FOR REAL.

1266
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:13,211
I GOT TO GO.

1267
00:50:14,979 --> 00:50:16,481
IT'S LIKE THAT?

1268
00:50:16,547 --> 00:50:17,948
JUST PUT THE MONEY
ON THE NIGHTSTAND

1269
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:20,185
AND BOUNCE?

1270
00:50:20,251 --> 00:50:21,486
LEAVE A BROTHER
HANGING?

1271
00:50:21,552 --> 00:50:22,720
BYE, DRE.

1272
00:50:22,787 --> 00:50:24,089
NO KISSING
ON THE FIRST DATE.

1273
00:50:24,155 --> 00:50:25,756
BYE, DRE.

1274
00:50:25,823 --> 00:50:27,392
Sidney, narrating:
JUST WHEN YOU THINK YOU KNOW

1275
00:50:27,458 --> 00:50:29,094
EVERYTHING THERE IS
TO KNOW ABOUT HIP-HOP

1276
00:50:29,160 --> 00:50:30,861
IT FINDS A WAY
TO SURPRISE YOU

1277
00:50:30,928 --> 00:50:32,630
AND REMIND YOU
WHY YOU FELL IN LOVE

1278
00:50:32,697 --> 00:50:34,365
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

1279
00:50:36,967 --> 00:50:38,069
GOOD EVENING,
MISS SHAW.

1280
00:50:38,136 --> 00:50:40,205
WELCOME
TO CHINGALLE'S.

1281
00:50:40,271 --> 00:50:41,172
HOW'D YOU KNOW
MY NAME?

1282
00:50:41,239 --> 00:50:42,707
PLEASE, THIS WAY.

1283
00:50:50,715 --> 00:50:52,517
Sidney: OH, MY GOODNESS.

1284
00:50:52,583 --> 00:50:53,784
THANK YOU.

1285
00:50:55,953 --> 00:50:57,288
THANK YOU,
JARMELLE.

1286
00:50:58,756 --> 00:51:00,391
PERFECT 10s.

1287
00:51:02,460 --> 00:51:03,394
THANK YOU.

1288
00:51:05,230 --> 00:51:06,464
WHOA, WHOA, EASY.

1289
00:51:06,531 --> 00:51:07,632
[LAUGHS]

1290
00:51:09,934 --> 00:51:11,769
THANK YOU.

1291
00:51:11,836 --> 00:51:12,870
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1292
00:51:12,937 --> 00:51:14,071
OK.

1293
00:51:28,186 --> 00:51:29,754
HEY, REESEY-PIECEY.

1294
00:51:30,988 --> 00:51:32,056
HI, BABY.

1295
00:51:32,123 --> 00:51:34,091
HOW YOU DOING?

1296
00:51:34,159 --> 00:51:35,193
HOW WAS YOUR DAY?

1297
00:51:35,260 --> 00:51:36,694
INTERESTING.

1298
00:51:41,566 --> 00:51:42,800
OH.

1299
00:51:42,867 --> 00:51:43,834
I FORGOT.

1300
00:51:43,901 --> 00:51:45,136
I TOOK YOUR PHONE AGAIN.

1301
00:51:45,203 --> 00:51:47,838
OH! YEAH, I KNOW. I KEPT
GETTING PHONE CALLS

1302
00:51:47,905 --> 00:51:49,140
FROM ALL
YOUR EX-GIRLFRIENDS.

1303
00:51:50,475 --> 00:51:51,576
HERE.

1304
00:51:51,642 --> 00:51:52,777
THANK YOU, BABY.

1305
00:51:53,878 --> 00:51:55,746
BABY...

1306
00:51:55,813 --> 00:51:57,014
MMM?

1307
00:51:57,081 --> 00:52:00,084
MMM...

1308
00:52:00,151 --> 00:52:03,921
I LOVE YOU...

1309
00:52:03,988 --> 00:52:05,823
AND, UH, AHEM...

1310
00:52:07,057 --> 00:52:09,194
I QUIT MY JOB TODAY.

1311
00:52:12,563 --> 00:52:13,831
WHY?

1312
00:52:13,898 --> 00:52:15,633
[SIGHS] 'CAUSE,
BABY, I JUST--

1313
00:52:15,700 --> 00:52:16,634
I NEEDED TO.

1314
00:52:16,701 --> 00:52:17,935
I HAD TO. I--

1315
00:52:18,002 --> 00:52:19,036
[SIGHS]

1316
00:52:19,103 --> 00:52:20,805
I'M GONNA START
MY OWN LABEL.

1317
00:52:20,871 --> 00:52:22,907
I'M GONNA DO
ALL THE THINGS

1318
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:24,275
THAT I'VE
EVER WANTED TO DO.

1319
00:52:24,342 --> 00:52:26,110
I THOUGHT YOU WERE DOING
ALL OF THAT AT MILLENNIUM.

1320
00:52:26,177 --> 00:52:29,314
NO, NOT AT MILLENNIUM.
I WASN'T.

1321
00:52:29,380 --> 00:52:32,750
I MEAN, YOU KNOW
HOW MUCH I LOVE MUSIC,

1322
00:52:32,817 --> 00:52:34,185
HOW MUCH I LOVE HIP-HOP,

1323
00:52:34,252 --> 00:52:35,253
HOW IT MAKES ME FEEL,
DRE--

1324
00:52:35,320 --> 00:52:36,287
AND I LOST THAT LOVE
AT MILLENNIUM.

1325
00:52:36,354 --> 00:52:37,688
HOW COULD YOU MAKE
A CHANGE LIKE THIS

1326
00:52:37,755 --> 00:52:39,089
WITHOUT CONSULTING ME?

1327
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:40,658
'CAUSE THIS IS SOMETHING
I HAD TO DO FOR ME.

1328
00:52:40,725 --> 00:52:42,460
PLUS, I KNOW
YOU WOULD'VE JUST TRIED

1329
00:52:42,527 --> 00:52:43,661
TO TALK ME
OUT OF IT, AND--

1330
00:52:43,728 --> 00:52:44,929
IT'S NOT FAIR
FOR YOU TO ASSUME THAT.

1331
00:52:44,995 --> 00:52:46,431
YOU DON'T KNOW THAT.
REESE,

1332
00:52:46,497 --> 00:52:48,366
YOU MEAN TO TELL ME,
HAD I TOLD YOU,

1333
00:52:48,433 --> 00:52:49,734
YOU WOULDN'T HAVE TRIED
TO TALK ME OUT OF IT?

1334
00:52:49,800 --> 00:52:51,469
YES, I WOULD HAVE TRIED
TO TALK YOU OUT OF IT,

1335
00:52:51,536 --> 00:52:52,870
BUT I'M SUPPOSED
TO DO THAT.

1336
00:52:52,937 --> 00:52:53,971
YOU GET SO EXCITED,

1337
00:52:54,038 --> 00:52:55,172
AND YOU DON'T
THINK STRAIGHT,

1338
00:52:55,240 --> 00:52:56,707
AND THEN YOU DO
SOMETHING LIKE THIS.

1339
00:52:56,774 --> 00:52:58,409
YOU CAN'T MAKE
A MAJOR LIFE DECISION

1340
00:52:58,476 --> 00:52:59,377
JUST BECAUSE
YOU FEEL LIKE IT--

1341
00:52:59,444 --> 00:53:01,746
I DON'T NEED YOU
TO BE MY LAWYER!

1342
00:53:06,717 --> 00:53:08,619
REESEY, I NEED YOU
TO BE MY WIFE.

1343
00:53:08,686 --> 00:53:10,521
AND A HUSBAND IS SUPPOSED
TO CONSULT HIS WIFE

1344
00:53:10,588 --> 00:53:11,656
WHEN HE CHANGES THE PLAN.

1345
00:53:11,722 --> 00:53:14,158
AND A WIFE
SUPPORTS HER HUSBAND!

1346
00:53:14,225 --> 00:53:16,694
BABY, I NEED
YOUR SUPPORT!

1347
00:53:19,230 --> 00:53:21,399
OK, FINE.

1348
00:53:23,368 --> 00:53:25,270
I SUPPORT YOU.

1349
00:53:25,336 --> 00:53:26,404
I'LL CALL
SOME MONEY PEOPLE.

1350
00:53:26,471 --> 00:53:27,972
WE'LL GET THIS
SQUARED AWAY.

1351
00:53:28,038 --> 00:53:29,407
THAT'S ALL TAKEN
CARE OF. UH...

1352
00:53:29,474 --> 00:53:31,309
SID SAID SHE'D HELP
OUT WITH SOME

1353
00:53:31,376 --> 00:53:32,510
OF THE INVESTING,
AND--

1354
00:53:32,577 --> 00:53:33,444
SIDNEY?

1355
00:53:33,511 --> 00:53:35,513
SIDNEY KNEW
ABOUT THIS BEFORE ME?

1356
00:53:35,580 --> 00:53:37,214
REESEY, BABY, PLEASE,
YOU KNOW SHE'S MY FRIEND--

1357
00:53:37,282 --> 00:53:39,750
YOUR FRIEND. [CLAPS] OK.

1358
00:53:39,817 --> 00:53:41,619
DAMN, DRE.
REESE.

1359
00:53:41,686 --> 00:53:43,053
WELL, I SEE YOU HAVE IT
ALL UNDER CONTROL.

1360
00:53:43,120 --> 00:53:44,021
I'M REALLY
HAPPY FOR YOU.

1361
00:53:44,088 --> 00:53:45,290
WHO, WHOA,
WHOA, WHOA.

1362
00:53:45,356 --> 00:53:46,357
SLOW YOUR ROLL.

1363
00:53:46,424 --> 00:53:47,458
REESEY! REESE!

1364
00:53:47,525 --> 00:53:48,793
NO, YOU SLOW
YOUR ROLL.

1365
00:53:48,859 --> 00:53:49,760
REESE!

1366
00:53:49,827 --> 00:53:50,961
DRE?

1367
00:53:51,028 --> 00:53:52,062
I'M FINE.

1368
00:53:52,129 --> 00:53:53,030
Sidney: YOU DID
ALL RIGHT. [LAUGHS]

1369
00:53:53,097 --> 00:53:54,064
Kelby:
JUST ALL RIGHT. OK.

1370
00:53:54,131 --> 00:53:55,165
SO--SO, YOU'RE USED

1371
00:53:55,232 --> 00:53:56,567
TO GUYS CLOSING
DOWN RESTAURANTS

1372
00:53:56,634 --> 00:53:58,469
ON THEIR BUSIEST
NIGHTS, HUH?

1373
00:53:58,536 --> 00:54:00,305
COMMANDEERING
THE KITCHEN,

1374
00:54:00,371 --> 00:54:01,672
SERVING YOU
LIKE A QUEEN.

1375
00:54:01,739 --> 00:54:03,274
YOU'RE USED
TO ALL THAT, HUH?

1376
00:54:03,341 --> 00:54:04,875
YOU BALLPLAYERS.
ALL RIGHT.

1377
00:54:04,942 --> 00:54:05,976
I DIDN'T THINK SO.

1378
00:54:06,043 --> 00:54:07,912
YOU THINK YOU'RE GONNA
GET SOME BOOTY, DON'T YOU?

1379
00:54:10,348 --> 00:54:11,282
WELL, YEAH.

1380
00:54:11,349 --> 00:54:13,217
YEAH?
[LAUGHS]

1381
00:54:13,284 --> 00:54:14,218
THAT'S THE PLAN.

1382
00:54:14,285 --> 00:54:15,286
ONE OF THESE DAYS.

1383
00:54:15,353 --> 00:54:17,021
COME ON, THAT'S WHAT
THIS IS ALL ABOUT.

1384
00:54:17,087 --> 00:54:18,255
YOU KNOW, THE DATING,

1385
00:54:18,323 --> 00:54:19,390
THE AWKWARD WALKS HOME.

1386
00:54:19,457 --> 00:54:20,791
THAT'S WHAT
MEN AND WOMEN DO.

1387
00:54:20,858 --> 00:54:22,059
YOU GOT IT ALL FIGURED
OUT, DON'T YOU?

1388
00:54:22,126 --> 00:54:23,528
I'M JUST TRYIN'
TO BE STRAIGHT UP.

1389
00:54:23,594 --> 00:54:24,495
[SIGHS]

1390
00:54:24,562 --> 00:54:25,696
YOU PUT A MAN
AND A WOMAN

1391
00:54:25,763 --> 00:54:27,465
TOGETHER
LONG ENOUGH, AND...

1392
00:54:27,532 --> 00:54:29,166
SOMETHING'S
GONNA GO DOWN.

1393
00:54:29,233 --> 00:54:30,568
WELL, WHAT MAKES
YOU THINK YOU GONNA BE

1394
00:54:30,635 --> 00:54:32,703
AROUND LONG ENOUGH
FOR SOMETHING TO GO DOWN?

1395
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:35,406
WELL, I THINK I GOT
A PRETTY GOOD SHOT.

1396
00:54:35,473 --> 00:54:36,607
IT'S NOT THAT GOOD.

1397
00:54:36,674 --> 00:54:38,709
ESPECIALLY
OUTSIDE 20 FEET.

1398
00:54:38,776 --> 00:54:41,111
AND YOU COULD WORK ON
THAT D A LITTLE, TOO.

1399
00:54:41,178 --> 00:54:42,179
OH, REALLY?
REALLY.

1400
00:54:42,246 --> 00:54:43,581
OK.

1401
00:54:43,648 --> 00:54:44,515
COME HERE.

1402
00:54:53,090 --> 00:54:56,026
HOW WAS THAT SHOT?

1403
00:54:56,093 --> 00:54:58,162
NOTHIN' BUT NET.

1404
00:54:58,228 --> 00:54:59,397
Dre: VICHON.
CHRIS VICHON.

1405
00:54:59,464 --> 00:55:00,765
V-I-C-H-O-N.

1406
00:55:00,831 --> 00:55:02,467
HE'S A DRIVER.

1407
00:55:02,533 --> 00:55:03,968
NO, NO, IT'S
NOT A COMPLAINT.

1408
00:55:04,034 --> 00:55:05,470
HE'S A DRIVER.

1409
00:55:05,536 --> 00:55:07,372
NEVER MIND. THANK YOU
FOR YOUR TIME.

1410
00:55:20,084 --> 00:55:23,153
[TELEPHONE RINGS]

1411
00:55:23,220 --> 00:55:24,589
