01:10:05,068 --> 01:10:06,002
WHY YOU TALKIN'
ALL LOUD, MAN?

1889
01:10:06,069 --> 01:10:07,003
YOU DON'T KNOW
WITH THIS PARTY.

1890
01:10:07,070 --> 01:10:08,004
THIS IS HOW RUMORS
GET STARTED.

1891
01:10:08,071 --> 01:10:09,406
WHAT'S WRONG
WITH YOU, MAN?

1892
01:10:09,473 --> 01:10:11,641
SO, YOU GONNA
GIVE HIM ANY PLAY?

1893
01:10:11,708 --> 01:10:13,377
I DON'T KNOW.
HE KIND OF YOUNG.

1894
01:10:13,443 --> 01:10:14,778
FIRST OF ALL, I AIN'T
SCARED OF WOMEN,

1895
01:10:14,844 --> 01:10:16,112
BUT I AIN'T LIKE YOU.

1896
01:10:16,179 --> 01:10:17,481
OK? I AIN'T
THE BLACK MALE MODEL.

1897
01:10:17,547 --> 01:10:19,182
I DON'T BE IN THE GYM
AT ALL TIMES.

1898
01:10:19,249 --> 01:10:20,350
FORGET IT, MAN. DON'T
EVEN SAY NOTHIN', MAN.

1899
01:10:20,417 --> 01:10:21,618
IT'S COOL. I GOT YOU.
I GOT YOU. LET'S GO.

1900
01:10:21,685 --> 01:10:22,786
YOU GONNA
HOOK ME UP, MAN?

1901
01:10:22,852 --> 01:10:23,787
DON'T PLAY ME, MAN.

1902
01:10:23,853 --> 01:10:25,522
Kelby: MENTOR!

1903
01:10:25,589 --> 01:10:27,357
[LAUGHING]

1904
01:10:27,424 --> 01:10:30,159
GOT MARRIAGE
ON MY MENU!

1905
01:10:30,226 --> 01:10:31,861
KELBY?

1906
01:10:31,928 --> 01:10:33,196
YOU KNOW
WHAT I THINK?

1907
01:10:33,263 --> 01:10:34,197
YOU SHOULD HIRE
A LAWYER

1908
01:10:34,264 --> 01:10:35,299
TO NEGOTIATE
YOUR CONTRACT.

1909
01:10:35,365 --> 01:10:36,500
YOU SERIOUS?
YEAH, I MEAN,

1910
01:10:36,566 --> 01:10:38,602
WHY PAY AN AGENT 4%
TO NEGOTIATE NUMBERS

1911
01:10:38,668 --> 01:10:40,970
THAT ARE ALREADY SET
BY A SALARY BASE CAP?

1912
01:10:41,037 --> 01:10:42,372
DRE, DON'T SAY ANYTHING.

1913
01:10:42,439 --> 01:10:43,707
QUIT WHILE WE STILL
HAVE A FRIENDSHIP.

1914
01:10:43,773 --> 01:10:45,475
HEY, THAT'S WHAT I'M
TRYIN' TO DO RIGHT NOW.

1915
01:10:45,542 --> 01:10:47,076
I'M TRYING TO SAVE
OUR FRIENDSHIP.

1916
01:10:47,143 --> 01:10:48,077
I'M WORRIED
ABOUT YOU.

1917
01:10:48,144 --> 01:10:49,212
WORRIED ABOUT ME?
YEAH!

1918
01:10:49,279 --> 01:10:50,314
YOU NEED TO STOP
WORRYING ABOUT ME

1919
01:10:50,380 --> 01:10:51,881
AND WORRY ABOUT
YOUR OWN MARRIAGE.

1920
01:10:51,948 --> 01:10:53,417
SO YOU'RE--
EXCUSE ME.

1921
01:10:53,483 --> 01:10:54,951
SO YOU'RE
THE ATTORNEY

1922
01:10:55,018 --> 01:10:56,152
I'M SUPPOSED
TO HIRE, RIGHT?

1923
01:10:56,219 --> 01:10:58,988
YEAH! VERY GOOD!
[LAUGHS]

1924
01:10:59,055 --> 01:10:59,989
Dre: MY MARRIAGE?

1925
01:11:00,056 --> 01:11:01,190
WHAT YOU MEAN?

1926
01:11:01,257 --> 01:11:02,158
WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

1927
01:11:02,225 --> 01:11:03,727
NOTHING. NOTHING.

1928
01:11:03,793 --> 01:11:05,161
SIDNEY.

1929
01:11:05,228 --> 01:11:06,630
WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

1930
01:11:06,696 --> 01:11:08,197
Kelby: MAYBE THIS
IS NOT THE BEST PLACE--

1931
01:11:08,264 --> 01:11:09,766
THE BEST TIME
TO TALK BUSINESS,

1932
01:11:09,833 --> 01:11:12,201
BUT I'M SURE WE'LL HAVE
PLENTY OF OPPORTUNITY

1933
01:11:12,268 --> 01:11:14,203
SINCE OUR SPOUSES
ARE BEST FRIENDS.

1934
01:11:14,270 --> 01:11:15,905
BEST--BEST FRIENDS.

1935
01:11:15,972 --> 01:11:17,106
THEY'RE SO CLOSE.

1936
01:11:17,173 --> 01:11:18,241
YEAH, WELL,
HOW--HOW DO YOU FEEL

1937
01:11:18,308 --> 01:11:19,376
WITH THEM BEING
SO CLOSE?

1938
01:11:19,443 --> 01:11:20,744
WELL, LET'S JUST
SAY IT'S VERY HARD

1939
01:11:20,810 --> 01:11:21,611
TO GET USED TO.

1940
01:11:21,678 --> 01:11:23,747
SIDNEY, WHAT DID
YOU MEAN?! SID--

1941
01:11:23,813 --> 01:11:26,182
CAN WE JUST
DROP THIS ALREADY?

1942
01:11:26,249 --> 01:11:27,250
TELL--

1943
01:11:27,317 --> 01:11:29,118
TELL ME
WHAT YOU MEANT.

1944
01:11:29,185 --> 01:11:30,219
NOTHING.
NO!

1945
01:11:30,286 --> 01:11:32,389
YOU SAID...

1946
01:11:32,456 --> 01:11:33,990
TE--
NOTHING.

1947
01:11:34,057 --> 01:11:35,659
JUST...

1948
01:11:35,725 --> 01:11:36,560
TELL ME.

1949
01:11:36,626 --> 01:11:38,261
ALL RIGHT. NOTHING.
IT'S NOTHING.

1950
01:11:38,328 --> 01:11:39,796
IT'S JUST I--I'VE
BEEN SEEING HER

1951
01:11:39,863 --> 01:11:42,699
AT THE GYM A LOT
LATELY, AND...[SIGHS]

1952
01:11:42,766 --> 01:11:44,534
A LOT OF GUYS TRY
AND RUN GAME ON HER,

1953
01:11:44,601 --> 01:11:46,202
AND, I DON'T KNOW,
SHE DON'T SEEM TO MIND.

1954
01:11:46,269 --> 01:11:48,505
HMM.

1955
01:11:48,572 --> 01:11:50,006
SHE'S A FLIRT.
ALL RIGHT?

1956
01:11:50,073 --> 01:11:51,140
SHE FLIRTS--
SHE FLIRTS A LOT.

1957
01:11:51,207 --> 01:11:52,442
SHE'S ALWAYS
BEEN A FLIRT.

1958
01:11:52,509 --> 01:11:54,744
AND SHE'S FLIRTED
WITH ME.

1959
01:11:54,811 --> 01:11:56,713
I'M COOL WITH THAT.
SHE FLIRT.

1960
01:11:56,780 --> 01:11:57,881
OK.

1961
01:11:57,947 --> 01:11:59,148
THAT'S WHAT I THOUGHT.

1962
01:11:59,215 --> 01:12:00,484
YOU'RE PROBABLY RIGHT.

1963
01:12:05,455 --> 01:12:07,691
IT'S WHEN YOU
TALK LIKE THAT,

1964
01:12:07,757 --> 01:12:08,892
THAT'S WHAT
MAKES ME THINK

1965
01:12:08,958 --> 01:12:10,026
THAT YOU'RE JEALOUS.

1966
01:12:10,093 --> 01:12:11,628
WHAT?!
YES.

1967
01:12:11,695 --> 01:12:13,229
JEALOUS!

1968
01:12:13,296 --> 01:12:14,498
NO WONDER YOU TWO
ARE MARRIED.

1969
01:12:14,564 --> 01:12:15,665
YOU'RE BOTH CRAZY!

1970
01:12:15,732 --> 01:12:16,666
LOOK HERE,

1971
01:12:16,733 --> 01:12:18,535
CONTRARY TO WHAT YOU
AND YOUR WIFE MAY THINK,

1972
01:12:18,602 --> 01:12:20,970
I DON'T SPEND MY NIGHTS
THINKIN' ABOUT YOU, OK?!

1973
01:12:21,037 --> 01:12:22,271
I GOT A MAN WHO'S FINE,

1974
01:12:22,338 --> 01:12:23,773
INTELLIGENT, SUCCESSFUL,
AND GIVES IT TO ME

1975
01:12:23,840 --> 01:12:25,274
ON A VERY,
VERY REGULAR BASIS,

1976
01:12:25,341 --> 01:12:27,043
AND THE SHIT
IS THE BOMB!

1977
01:12:28,545 --> 01:12:30,514
SO? I DON'T
CARE WHAT--

1978
01:12:30,580 --> 01:12:32,549
DRE, I NEED YOU
TO BE HAPPY FOR ME.

1979
01:12:32,616 --> 01:12:34,484
I NEED YOU TO BE
THERE FOR ME,

1980
01:12:34,551 --> 01:12:36,152
JUST LIKE
YOU ASKED OF ME.

1981
01:12:36,219 --> 01:12:37,754
SO--SO I CAN HAVE TEA

1982
01:12:37,821 --> 01:12:40,857
AND EAT CUCUMBER SANDWICHES
WITH THE CRUST CUT OFF!

1983
01:12:40,924 --> 01:12:42,826
[LAUGHING]

1984
01:12:49,466 --> 01:12:50,700
[LAUGHS]

1985
01:12:55,905 --> 01:12:57,907
[LAUGHS]

1986
01:12:57,974 --> 01:12:59,242
I'M SORRY.

1987
01:12:59,308 --> 01:13:01,445
I'M SORRY. AHEM.

1988
01:13:01,511 --> 01:13:04,414
YOU'RE UPSET.
I'M SORRY.

1989
01:13:04,481 --> 01:13:07,784
I'M, UH--

1990
01:13:07,851 --> 01:13:09,085
FOR REAL...

1991
01:13:09,152 --> 01:13:10,920
I'M, UH--
I'M HAPPY FOR YOU.

1992
01:13:10,987 --> 01:13:12,188
I'M HAPPY FOR YOU.
I'M HAPPY FOR YOU,

1993
01:13:12,255 --> 01:13:14,991
JUST LIKE YOU WAS
HAPPY FOR ME.

1994
01:13:15,058 --> 01:13:16,626
ALL RIGHT?

1995
01:13:16,693 --> 01:13:18,595
COOL?

1996
01:13:18,662 --> 01:13:20,530
ALL RIGHT,
CAN I GET A HUG?

1997
01:13:29,573 --> 01:13:32,075
GOOD FRIENDS.

1998
01:13:33,843 --> 01:13:35,979
YOU TORE UP
THOSE COOKIES.

1999
01:13:39,415 --> 01:13:40,550
* OO-OOH *

2000
01:13:40,617 --> 01:13:45,354
* OOH *

2001
01:13:45,421 --> 01:13:46,523
* OO-OOH *

2002
01:13:46,590 --> 01:13:48,357
* OOH *

2003
01:13:48,424 --> 01:13:51,360
* OOH--OOH *

2004
01:13:51,427 --> 01:13:52,529
* OO-OOH *

2005
01:13:52,596 --> 01:13:54,798
* OOH *

2006
01:14:04,708 --> 01:14:05,842
Sidney: NICE SHOT.

2007
01:14:05,909 --> 01:14:06,876
HEY, BEAUTIFUL.

2008
01:14:06,943 --> 01:14:07,877
HEY.

2009
01:14:07,944 --> 01:14:09,112
MMM...

2010
01:14:11,347 --> 01:14:12,215
WHAT YOU GOT THERE?

2011
01:14:12,281 --> 01:14:14,317
I, UH...

2012
01:14:14,383 --> 01:14:16,085
WANTED US TO MAKE
THE FINAL DECISION

2013
01:14:16,152 --> 01:14:17,120
ON THESE INVITES.

2014
01:14:17,186 --> 01:14:18,688
ALL RIGHT.

2015
01:14:18,755 --> 01:14:20,189
WELL, WHATEVER YOU WANT
IS COOL WITH ME.

2016
01:14:21,558 --> 01:14:23,693
IT'S ALL YOU.

2017
01:14:27,196 --> 01:14:28,197
WHAT'S WRONG?

2018
01:14:29,833 --> 01:14:31,735
I JUST NEEDED
A WRITING BREAK.

2019
01:14:31,801 --> 01:14:33,302
OH.

2020
01:14:33,369 --> 01:14:35,805
I MEAN, WRITIN'
THESE ARTICLES

2021
01:14:35,872 --> 01:14:38,207
HERE AND THERE
IS ONE THING, BUT...

2022
01:14:38,274 --> 01:14:39,475
THIS BOOK IS DIFFERENT.

2023
01:14:39,543 --> 01:14:41,878
I REALLY WANT IT
TO BE GOOD, YOU KNOW?

2024
01:14:41,945 --> 01:14:43,246
YEAH.

2025
01:14:43,312 --> 01:14:44,748
AND, UH...

2026
01:14:44,814 --> 01:14:47,183
I DON'T KNOW IF I CAN
WRITE AT THAT LEVEL.

2027
01:14:47,250 --> 01:14:49,152
OF COURSE YOU CAN!

2028
01:14:49,218 --> 01:14:51,354
CAN I ASK YOU
SOMETHING?

2029
01:14:51,420 --> 01:14:52,622
YEAH.

2030
01:14:52,689 --> 01:14:54,057
WHAT DID YOU THINK OF
THE UNDERGROUND REVIEW

2031
01:14:54,123 --> 01:14:56,459
I WROTE ON CASSIUS
IN LAST MONTH'S ISSUE?

2032
01:14:56,526 --> 01:14:58,161
THAT WAS GOOD.

2033
01:14:58,227 --> 01:14:59,128
THAT WAS REALLY GOOD.

2034
01:14:59,195 --> 01:15:01,297
REALLY?
YEAH.

2035
01:15:01,364 --> 01:15:02,265
WHAT WAS GOOD
ABOUT IT?

2036
01:15:03,499 --> 01:15:05,635
YOU KNOW, EVERYTHING.
I MEAN, THE--

2037
01:15:05,702 --> 01:15:07,370
YEAH, THE WHOLE--
THE WHOLE THING WAS GREAT.

2038
01:15:07,436 --> 01:15:08,605
IT WAS REALLY GOOD.

2039
01:15:10,774 --> 01:15:11,941
YOU DIDN'T READ IT,
DID YOU?

2040
01:15:12,008 --> 01:15:14,343
WHAT?

2041
01:15:14,410 --> 01:15:16,680
OH, YEAH, NO. UM...

2042
01:15:16,746 --> 01:15:18,915
WHAT ABOUT THE ONE
BEFORE THAT?

2043
01:15:18,982 --> 01:15:22,051
UH...

2044
01:15:22,118 --> 01:15:23,720
WELL, THE ONE YOU WROTE
ABOUT ME WAS GREAT.

2045
01:15:24,854 --> 01:15:26,055
[LAUGHS]

2046
01:15:27,290 --> 01:15:28,658
HEY, I'M SORRY.

2047
01:15:28,725 --> 01:15:30,459
LOOK--LOOK...

2048
01:15:30,526 --> 01:15:32,762
I'VE BEEN ON THE ROAD.

2049
01:15:32,829 --> 01:15:34,798
YOU KNOW HOW IT GOES.

2050
01:15:34,864 --> 01:15:37,466
LOOK, I PROMISE I WILL
READ EVERY ARTICLE

2051
01:15:37,533 --> 01:15:39,302
YOU'VE EVER WRITTEN
IN YOUR LIFE.

2052
01:15:39,368 --> 01:15:40,503
EVERYTHING.

2053
01:15:40,570 --> 01:15:42,338
LIKE YOUR ESSAYS,
YOUR LITTLE LOVE LETTERS,

2054
01:15:42,405 --> 01:15:43,472
EVERYTHING.

2055
01:15:43,539 --> 01:15:45,474
OK? EVERY SINGLE THING.

2056
01:15:45,541 --> 01:15:46,943
FOR YOU.
[BUZZER]

2057
01:15:47,010 --> 01:15:48,477
ALL RIGHT, I GOTTA GO,
MS. DAWSON.

2058
01:15:48,544 --> 01:15:49,846
OH! OH, MY BAD.

2059
01:15:49,913 --> 01:15:51,815
[LAUGHS]

2060
01:15:51,881 --> 01:15:53,016
SEE YOU.

2061
01:15:54,584 --> 01:15:56,753
[MUSIC PLAYING]

2062
01:16:02,525 --> 01:16:04,894
SO, THIS IS WHERE
MY MONEY'S GOING?

2063
01:16:04,961 --> 01:16:09,065
HA HA. THAT'S CALLED
BRAIN FOOD RIGHT THERE.

2064
01:16:09,132 --> 01:16:12,035
[CELL PHONE RINGS]

2065
01:16:16,439 --> 01:16:18,307
RICHARD? WHO'S RICHARD?

2066
01:16:23,279 --> 01:16:24,347
[TURNS OFF MUSIC]

2067
01:16:24,413 --> 01:16:25,481
YO, CHRIS.

2068
01:16:25,548 --> 01:16:26,549
WHAT'S UP?

2069
01:16:26,616 --> 01:16:27,851
YOU GOT YOUR CAB
WITH YOU?

2070
01:16:29,152 --> 01:16:30,319
WAIT A MINUTE.

2071
01:16:30,386 --> 01:16:31,721
DRE.

2072
01:16:33,522 --> 01:16:35,992
DRE.

2073
01:16:38,127 --> 01:16:40,129
Sidney: OH, NO.

2074
01:16:41,564 --> 01:16:42,966
THAT GUY GOES TO OUR GYM.

2075
01:16:43,032 --> 01:16:45,769
DRE, THINK ABOUT THIS, OK?
LET'S JUST GO.

2076
01:16:45,835 --> 01:16:47,971
[SIGHS] DRE, YOU DON'T
WANT TO DO THIS.

2077
01:16:49,773 --> 01:16:51,207
Dre: WHAT'S UP?
SURPRISE!

2078
01:16:51,274 --> 01:16:52,909
REESEY, WHAT--

2079
01:16:52,976 --> 01:16:54,143
HUH--YOU--

2080
01:16:54,210 --> 01:16:56,045
HOW--ARE YOU DOIN'?

2081
01:16:56,112 --> 01:16:57,513
HEY...

2082
01:16:57,580 --> 01:16:59,615
HEY...
HEY...

2083
01:16:59,683 --> 01:17:01,117
GUYS, WHAT'S UP?

2084
01:17:01,184 --> 01:17:02,919
HOW ARE YOU DOIN'?

2085
01:17:02,986 --> 01:17:03,953
HA HA...

2086
01:17:04,020 --> 01:17:05,789
IT'S FUNNY RUNNIN'
INTO YOU HERE,

2087
01:17:05,855 --> 01:17:07,523
SINGING LOVE SONGS
TO EACH OTHER.

2088
01:17:07,590 --> 01:17:08,825
DRE...

2089
01:17:08,892 --> 01:17:10,159
SHIT, THAT WAS PRETTY.
DON'T STOP ON MY ACCOUNT.

2090
01:17:10,226 --> 01:17:11,194
OH, DRE...

2091
01:17:11,260 --> 01:17:12,662
YEAH. ME AND SID,

2092
01:17:12,729 --> 01:17:14,163
WE WAS JUST
IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD.

2093
01:17:14,230 --> 01:17:15,464
WE THOUGHT--YOU MIND
IF WE JOIN YOU?

2094
01:17:15,531 --> 01:17:16,700
NO, NOT AT ALL.
NOT AT ALL.

2095
01:17:16,766 --> 01:17:18,267
Richard: HAVE A SEAT, MAN.

2096
01:17:18,334 --> 01:17:20,336
RIGHT.
SIT DOWN, GIRL.

2097
01:17:20,403 --> 01:17:21,570
WHY YOU ALL STIFF?

2098
01:17:21,637 --> 01:17:22,739
REESEY...

2099
01:17:22,806 --> 01:17:24,774
I SEE YOU GOT ON MY...

2100
01:17:24,841 --> 01:17:25,875
FAVORITE DRESS

2101
01:17:25,942 --> 01:17:27,543
WITH THIS AREA
ALL, LIKE, "HEY."

2102
01:17:27,610 --> 01:17:28,611
ALL OUT.

2103
01:17:28,678 --> 01:17:30,346
GREASED UP FOR MY MAN.

2104
01:17:30,413 --> 01:17:31,514
I'M SORRY. DRE ELLIS.
YOU ARE?

2105
01:17:31,580 --> 01:17:32,982
RICHARD LAWSON.

2106
01:17:33,049 --> 01:17:34,483
[IMITATING HIM]
RICHARD LAWSON.

2107
01:17:34,550 --> 01:17:35,852
ALL RIGHT.
YOU SOUND EDUCATED.

2108
01:17:35,919 --> 01:17:37,053
GOOD FOR YOU, GIRL.

2109
01:17:37,120 --> 01:17:38,487
I, UM...

2110
01:17:38,554 --> 01:17:39,588
YOU GUYS, UM,

2111
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:40,724
FRIENDS OF REESE'S?

2112
01:17:40,790 --> 01:17:42,158
YEAH, WELL, ACTUALLY,

2113
01:17:42,225 --> 01:17:44,260
THE FUNNY THING IS,
SHE'S MY WIFE.

2114
01:17:44,327 --> 01:17:46,229
WHAT?

2115
01:17:46,295 --> 01:17:48,898
Richard: OH...

2116
01:17:48,965 --> 01:17:50,800
LOOK, HEY, I'M SORRY.
I DIDN'T--

2117
01:17:50,867 --> 01:17:51,735
THAT'S COOL.
THAT'S COOL.

2118
01:17:51,801 --> 01:17:52,869
HOW COULD YOU KNOW?

2119
01:17:52,936 --> 01:17:55,872
SHE AIN'T WEARING
THE $15,000 RING

2120
01:17:55,939 --> 01:17:57,073
THAT I BOUGHT HER ASS.

2121
01:17:57,140 --> 01:17:58,074
I'M STILL PAYING IT OFF,
BUT YOU UNDERSTAND.

2122
01:17:58,141 --> 01:18:00,109
ACTUALLY,
I'M PAYING FOR IT.

2123
01:18:00,176 --> 01:18:01,778
COULD YOU NOT PUT MY
BUSINESS OUT ON THE STREET?

2124
01:18:01,845 --> 01:18:03,212
WILL YOU BE JOINING US
FOR DINNER?

2125
01:18:03,279 --> 01:18:04,213
LISTEN, MY MAN--

2126
01:18:04,280 --> 01:18:05,681
YOU KNOW WHAT?
WE WERE JUST ABOUT TO LEAVE.

2127
01:18:05,749 --> 01:18:07,116
I'M TRYING TO ORDER
THE MOST EXPENSIVE

2128
01:18:07,183 --> 01:18:09,285
BOTTLE OF CHAMPAGNE,
'CAUSE WE FIXIN' TO CELEBRATE.

2129
01:18:09,352 --> 01:18:10,386
DRE.

2130
01:18:10,453 --> 01:18:12,155
WE GONNA CELEBRATE WHAT?
[TAPS SPOON ON GLASS]

2131
01:18:12,221 --> 01:18:14,157
* MY DIVORCE *
HOW ABOUT THAT?

2132
01:18:14,223 --> 01:18:15,558
AND SOME PORK CHOPS.

2133
01:18:15,624 --> 01:18:16,960
DRE, COME ON.

2134
01:18:17,026 --> 01:18:17,961
'CAUSE I'M KIND OF HUNGRY.
ALL RIGHT?

2135
01:18:18,027 --> 01:18:19,362
YOU'RE MAKING A SCENE.

2136
01:18:19,428 --> 01:18:20,663
GOOD. I WANT TO MAKE A SCENE.
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYIN'?

2137
01:18:20,730 --> 01:18:21,664
BYE-BYE, RICHARD LAWSON.

2138
01:18:21,731 --> 01:18:24,100
Sidney:
THIS IS SO EMBARRASSING.

2139
01:18:24,167 --> 01:18:25,969
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU GOT ME TO DO THAT.

2140
01:18:26,035 --> 01:18:27,203
HEY, STOP COMPLAINING.

2141
01:18:27,270 --> 01:18:29,038
YOU FORGET IT WAS ME
WHO HELPED YOU

2142
01:18:29,105 --> 01:18:31,074
LET ALL THE AIR OUT OF
SHAWN'S TIRES

2143
01:18:31,140 --> 01:18:32,842
WHEN HE ASKED ANGIE
TO THE HOMECOMING DANCE

2144
01:18:32,909 --> 01:18:34,443
INSTEAD OF YOU.

2145
01:18:34,510 --> 01:18:35,845
KEY WORD: HOME...COMING.

2146
01:18:35,912 --> 01:18:38,181
HIGH SCHOOL. WE'RE ALMOST
30 YEARS OLD, DRE.

2147
01:18:38,247 --> 01:18:39,648
[SIGHS]

2148
01:18:39,715 --> 01:18:41,350
OH, TIME IS A BITCH.

2149
01:18:41,417 --> 01:18:44,187
I SWEAR, I STILL FEEL LIKE
WE'RE JUST THOSE 2 KIDS

2150
01:18:44,253 --> 01:18:46,255
POP-LOCKING
AT THE BLOCK PARTIES.

2151
01:18:46,322 --> 01:18:48,524
YOU REMEMBER MY FIRST
LITTLE BEAT MACHINE?

2152
01:18:48,591 --> 01:18:50,293
BOY, YOU THOUGHT
YOU WERE D-NICE.

2153
01:18:50,359 --> 01:18:53,062
THE TR-808.

2154
01:18:53,129 --> 01:18:54,597
BUST THIS.

2155
01:18:54,663 --> 01:18:55,899
[CLEARS THROAT]

2156
01:18:55,965 --> 01:18:58,567
"SIMPLICITY PROVIDES

2157
01:18:58,634 --> 01:19:00,436
"A FINE LINE
BETWEEN ELOQUENCE

2158
01:19:00,503 --> 01:19:01,737
AND PLAINNESS."

2159
01:19:02,939 --> 01:19:04,707
THAT'S A DOPE LINE.

2160
01:19:04,774 --> 01:19:07,610
AND I KNOW LL DIDN'T THINK
HE WAS THAT DEEP.

2161
01:19:07,676 --> 01:19:10,613
THAT WAS MY FIRST
PUBLISHED ARTICLE.

2162
01:19:10,679 --> 01:19:12,648
I CAN'T WAIT
FOR YOUR BOOK TO COME OUT.

2163
01:19:12,715 --> 01:19:14,717
AND WHEN YOU LEFT,

2164
01:19:14,784 --> 01:19:16,953
I WENT OUT,

2165
01:19:17,020 --> 01:19:19,722
GOT THE L.A. TIMES,
EVERY WEDNESDAY,

2166
01:19:19,789 --> 01:19:21,925
FOR YOUR COLUMN.

2167
01:19:21,991 --> 01:19:24,293
I'D GO TO THE PARK
AND READ IT.

2168
01:19:24,360 --> 01:19:26,095
I DON'T KNOW, IT JUST...

2169
01:19:27,530 --> 01:19:30,099
MADE ME FEEL CLOSER TO YOU.

2170
01:19:33,336 --> 01:19:34,403
UH...

2171
01:19:34,470 --> 01:19:37,073
YOU WANT ANYTHING?

2172
01:19:37,140 --> 01:19:38,307
COFFEE?

2173
01:19:38,374 --> 01:19:39,542
VODKA?
UH, NO.

2174
01:19:39,608 --> 01:19:40,810
I WANTED THEM PORK CHOPS.

2175
01:19:40,877 --> 01:19:42,078
I TOLD YOU WE SHOULD HAVE
STAYED FOR DINNER.

2176
01:19:42,145 --> 01:19:44,814
HOW CAN YOU...
JOKE ABOUT THIS?

2177
01:19:44,881 --> 01:19:46,515
'CAUSE I WOULD BE
FLIPPING OUT.

2178
01:19:46,582 --> 01:19:47,516
HA HA!

2179
01:19:48,784 --> 01:19:50,686
SID, I DO NOT KNOW.

2180
01:19:50,753 --> 01:19:52,889
I GUESS I'LL BREAK DOWN
LATER.

2181
01:19:52,956 --> 01:19:54,423
YOU KNOW WHAT, THOUGH?
I--I--

2182
01:19:54,490 --> 01:19:56,325
I'M GLAD I KNOW NOW.

2183
01:19:56,392 --> 01:19:59,829
I GUESS I ALWAYS KNEW
DEEP DOWN INSIDE

2184
01:19:59,896 --> 01:20:01,664
THAT WE WEREN'T
MEANT TO BE TOGETHER.

2185
01:20:01,730 --> 01:20:02,698
YEAH?

2186
01:20:02,765 --> 01:20:03,933
MM.

2187
01:20:04,000 --> 01:20:06,369
AND WHEN DID YOU
FIGURE THAT OUT?

2188
01:20:07,703 --> 01:20:09,405
THE NIGHT BEFORE THE WEDDING.

2189
01:20:11,407 --> 01:20:12,842
SOMETHING HAPPENED

2190
01:20:12,909 --> 01:20:16,412
BETWEEN ME LEAVING THE HOUSE...

2191
01:20:16,479 --> 01:20:18,281
AND, UH...

2192
01:20:19,648 --> 01:20:21,985
GETTING TO THE WEDDING.

2193
01:20:22,051 --> 01:20:24,053
BUT, YOU KNOW,
I SHOOK IT OFF,

2194
01:20:24,120 --> 01:20:26,455
'CAUSE, DAMN,
I HAD A BEAUTIFUL WOMAN

2195
01:20:26,522 --> 01:20:28,925
THAT LOVED ME TO DEATH.

2196
01:20:28,992 --> 01:20:31,594
SO, YOU KNOW,
I TOOK ALL THOSE FEELINGS

2197
01:20:31,660 --> 01:20:33,629
AND...LOCKED THEM AWAY,

2198
01:20:33,696 --> 01:20:38,935
'CAUSE NOT EVERYBODY
CAN MARRY THEIR ONE TRUE LOVE.

2199
01:20:39,002 --> 01:20:41,437
IT WAS A PRETTY DIFFICULT
SITUATION.

2200
01:20:41,504 --> 01:20:43,639
DO YOU, UH...

2201
01:20:43,706 --> 01:20:47,443
YOU KNOW ANYBODY
LIKE THAT?

2202
01:20:47,510 --> 01:20:48,677
NO, I DON'T.

2203
01:20:48,744 --> 01:20:50,279
NO?

2204
01:20:50,346 --> 01:20:52,348
BUT...

2205
01:20:52,415 --> 01:20:54,050
I DO KNOW SOMEBODY

2206
01:20:54,117 --> 01:20:56,019
THAT WAS FRIENDS
WITH THIS GUY

2207
01:20:56,085 --> 01:20:58,821
A LONG TIME, AND...

2208
01:20:58,888 --> 01:21:01,724
SHE THOUGHT MAYBE
IT WAS MORE THAN JUST...

2209
01:21:01,790 --> 01:21:03,359
FRIENDS, BUT...

2210
01:21:03,426 --> 01:21:06,795
SOMETHING HAPPENED
TO HER, COINCIDENTALLY,

2211
01:21:06,862 --> 01:21:07,863
BEFORE YOUR WEDDING.

2212
01:21:07,931 --> 01:21:09,966
OH, YEAH?

2213
01:21:10,033 --> 01:21:12,568
AND...SHE REALIZED
IT WAS NOTHING MORE

2214
01:21:12,635 --> 01:21:13,669
THAN JUST FRIENDS.

2215
01:21:13,736 --> 01:21:14,803
NOTHING?

2216
01:21:14,870 --> 01:21:16,272
NOTHING.

2217
01:21:16,339 --> 01:21:17,306
JUST FRIENDS?

2218
01:21:17,373 --> 01:21:18,207
JUST FRIENDS.

2219
01:21:23,546 --> 01:21:27,283
Sidney: I CAN'T BELIEVE
WHAT JUST HAPPENED.

2220
01:21:27,350 --> 01:21:28,351
Dre: I KNOW.

2221
01:21:29,953 --> 01:21:31,921
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO SAY.

2222
01:21:35,291 --> 01:21:38,561
I MEAN, USUALLY I'M LIKE
THE ENERGIZER BUNNY.

2223
01:21:38,627 --> 01:21:39,895
YOU KNOW.

2224
01:21:39,963 --> 01:21:41,998
I KEEP GOIN' AND GOIN'--

2225
01:21:42,065 --> 01:21:44,300
I WAS TALKING
ABOUT US...

2226
01:21:44,367 --> 01:21:45,301
DOING IT.

2227
01:21:47,070 --> 01:21:49,772
THIS WAS BAD.

2228
01:21:49,838 --> 01:21:53,209
WE MADE A HUGE MISTAKE.

2229
01:21:53,276 --> 01:21:55,945
HONEY, I SAID I WAS SORRY.

2230
01:21:56,012 --> 01:21:58,781
I MEAN, NEXT TIME I WON'T
BE SO CAUGHT OFF-GUARD.

2231
01:21:58,847 --> 01:22:00,149
I'LL USE A LITTLE GINSENG.

2232
01:22:00,216 --> 01:22:02,018
THERE ISN'T GONNA BE
A NEXT TIME. DON'T YOU GET IT?

2233
01:22:02,085 --> 01:22:04,720
THIS WAS BAD.
REAL, REAL BAD.

2234
01:22:04,787 --> 01:22:06,155
IT COULDN'T HAVE BEEN
THAT BAD.

2235
01:22:06,222 --> 01:22:07,991
DRE, I'M NOT TALKING
ABOUT THAT.

2236
01:22:08,057 --> 01:22:09,558
I'M GETTING MARRIED.
YOU'RE STILL MARRIED.

2237
01:22:09,625 --> 01:22:11,961
AND WE--WE JUST GOT BUSY.

2238
01:22:12,028 --> 01:22:13,029
WHERE ARE MY SHOES?

2239
01:22:13,096 --> 01:22:14,163
THEY'RE DOWNSTAIRS.

2240
01:22:14,230 --> 01:22:15,564
WAIT. WHERE YOU GOIN'?

2241
01:22:15,631 --> 01:22:16,699
THIS IS YOUR SPOT.

2242
01:22:16,765 --> 01:22:18,167
I NEED TO GET MYSELF
TOGETHER.

2243
01:22:18,234 --> 01:22:20,403
I HAVE TO MEET KELBY
AFTER THE GAME.

2244
01:22:20,469 --> 01:22:23,139
WAIT. YOU'RE NOT GONNA
TELL HIM, ARE YOU?

2245
01:22:23,206 --> 01:22:24,807
WHAT ARE YOU GONNA
TELL HIM?

2246
01:22:24,873 --> 01:22:25,941
ARE YOU GONNA TELL HIM?

2247
01:22:26,009 --> 01:22:27,310
I DON'T KNOW.
I--I--I--

2248
01:22:27,376 --> 01:22:29,178
NO, I'M NOT.
I'M NOT. I'M--

2249
01:22:29,245 --> 01:22:30,946
HE DOESN'T KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED

2250
01:22:31,014 --> 01:22:33,316
AND I WANT TO
KEEP IT THAT WAY.

2251
01:22:33,382 --> 01:22:35,051
WELL,
YOU'RE NOT GONNA...

2252
01:22:35,118 --> 01:22:36,885
ARE YOU STILL
GONNA MARRY THIS CAT

2253
01:22:36,952 --> 01:22:38,287
AFTER WHAT
WE JUST HAD?

2254
01:22:38,354 --> 01:22:40,323
DRE...

2255
01:22:40,389 --> 01:22:42,725
WHAT JUST HAPPENED
WAS THE MOST...

2256
01:22:42,791 --> 01:22:44,127
AMAZING...

2257
01:22:44,193 --> 01:22:46,929
MOST FULFILLING...

2258
01:22:46,996 --> 01:22:48,864
MOST EXHILARATING...

2259
01:22:48,931 --> 01:22:51,867
5 MINUTES I'VE EVER HAD
IN MY LIFE.

2260
01:22:51,934 --> 01:22:53,069
7.
10 MINUTES.

2261
01:22:53,136 --> 01:22:54,803
9?
OK, 8, WHATEVER.

2262
01:22:54,870 --> 01:22:56,739
THE POINT IS,

2263
01:22:56,805 --> 01:22:58,141
WHAT DO WE DO NOW?

2264
01:22:58,207 --> 01:23:00,076
WE CAN'T JUST GO BACK
TO THE WAY THINGS WERE.

2265
01:23:00,143 --> 01:23:01,577
WAIT, WAIT.

2266
01:23:02,945 --> 01:23:04,847
WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

2267
01:23:04,913 --> 01:23:06,282
I NEED SPACE.

2268
01:23:06,349 --> 01:23:08,517
US STAYING SO CLOSE, SPENDING
SO MUCH TIME TOGETHER,

2269
01:23:08,584 --> 01:23:10,453
JUST CONFUSES THINGS
FOR ME RIGHT NOW.

2270
01:23:10,519 --> 01:23:12,921
AND BESIDES,
WE WOULDN'T EVEN BE HERE

2271
01:23:12,988 --> 01:23:14,223
IF IT WASN'T FOR YOU
CATCHING REESE.

2272
01:23:14,290 --> 01:23:15,924
WHY ARE YOU TALKING
LIKE THAT?

2273
01:23:15,991 --> 01:23:17,860
WHY DOES IT HAVE TO BE
ALL OR NOTHING?

2274
01:23:17,926 --> 01:23:19,628
BECAUSE WE BOTH KNOW

2275
01:23:19,695 --> 01:23:21,697
IT'S THE RIGHT THING TO DO.

2276
01:23:23,766 --> 01:23:25,868
[MUSIC PLAYING]

2277
01:23:25,934 --> 01:23:29,338
[OVERLAPPING CONVERSATIONS]

2278
01:23:29,405 --> 01:23:30,839
[SIGHS]

2279
01:23:30,906 --> 01:23:32,708
HEY.

2280
01:24:07,843 --> 01:24:10,113
[OVERLAPPING CONVERSATIONS]

2281
01:24:17,353 --> 01:24:19,422
I KNOW YOU'VE DONE THIS
MAD TIMES.

2282
01:24:19,488 --> 01:24:21,457
I KNOW YOU KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

2283
01:24:21,524 --> 01:24:22,591
BUT, YOU KNOW,
WHEN YOU GO IN THERE,

2284
01:24:22,658 --> 01:24:23,859
JUST, YOU KNOW,
BE FIRM WITH THEM,

2285
01:24:23,926 --> 01:24:24,827
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYIN'?

2286
01:24:24,893 --> 01:24:25,928
YEAH.

2287
01:24:25,994 --> 01:24:28,131
DON'T PUNK OUT
LIKE YOU DID WITH SIDNEY.

2288
01:24:28,197 --> 01:24:29,332
JUST...
YOU STAND YOUR GROUND.

2289
01:24:29,398 --> 01:24:31,400
I NEVER PUNK OUT
WITH SIDNEY.

2290
01:24:31,467 --> 01:24:32,368
YOU DID.

2291
01:24:32,435 --> 01:24:34,437
ALL I DID
WAS RESPECT HER WISHES.

2292
01:24:34,503 --> 01:24:36,105
SOUND LIKE SOME PUNK LOGIC
RIGHT THERE.

2293
01:24:36,172 --> 01:24:37,273
HOW YOU FIGURE?
WHAT ABOUT FRANCINE?

2294
01:24:37,340 --> 01:24:38,941
YOU WERE FEELING HER,
RIGHT?

2295
01:24:39,007 --> 01:24:40,243
YEAH.

2296
01:24:40,309 --> 01:24:41,310
YOU AIN'T DOIN' NOTHIN'
ABOUT IT.

2297
01:24:41,377 --> 01:24:43,646
I'M NOT...
THE HUMPHREY BOGART IN THIS.

2298
01:24:43,712 --> 01:24:45,948
I'M THE PETER LORRE.
I'M THE SIDEKICK CHARACTER.

2299
01:24:46,014 --> 01:24:47,350
YOU THE HUMPHREY BOGART.

2300
01:24:47,416 --> 01:24:49,518
YOU HAD YOUR OPENING.
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYING?

2301
01:24:49,585 --> 01:24:52,020
SHE WANTED YOU TO STOP HER
FROM MARRYING THE OLD DUDE,

2302
01:24:52,087 --> 01:24:54,223
BUT YOU LET IT RIDE,
YOU KNOW?

2303
01:24:54,290 --> 01:24:56,192
SAME THING BOGEY DID, MAN.
YOU'RE THE SAME DUDE.

2304
01:24:56,259 --> 01:24:58,661
MAN, DON'T BE DISSIN'
HUMPHREY BOGART, MAN.

2305
01:24:58,727 --> 01:25:00,062
WHY NOT?

2306
01:25:00,129 --> 01:25:01,864
'CAUSE HE'S HUMPHREY BOGART.
HE'S THE MAN.

2307
01:25:01,930 --> 01:25:03,399
YO, HE WAS FIGHTIN'
A WAR.

2308
01:25:03,466 --> 01:25:04,533
THAT'S WHAT THEY DID
BACK THEN.

2309
01:25:04,600 --> 01:25:05,634
YOU KNOW WHAT HE NEEDED
TO DO BACK THEN?

2310
01:25:05,701 --> 01:25:08,471
HE NEEDED TO STOP
FINE-ASS INGRID BERGMAN

2311
01:25:08,537 --> 01:25:11,073
FROM GETTIN' ON THE PLANE
WITH THE CORNY DUDE.

2312
01:25:11,140 --> 01:25:13,075
AND THEN,

2313
01:25:13,142 --> 01:25:15,744
HE GONNA WALK OFF
IN THE FOG

2314
01:25:15,811 --> 01:25:16,845
WITH SOME OTHER DUDE.

2315
01:25:16,912 --> 01:25:18,881
COME ON, MAN.

2316
01:25:18,947 --> 01:25:21,484
WITH ANOTHER DUDE,
IN THE FOG?

2317
01:25:23,018 --> 01:25:25,188
COME ON. 2 GROWN MEN
WALK OFF IN A FOG,

2318
01:25:25,254 --> 01:25:26,655
YOU DON'T KNOW
WHERE THEY GOIN'?

2319
01:25:28,991 --> 01:25:30,459
THINK ABOUT IT, MAN.

2320
01:25:30,526 --> 01:25:32,361
YOU SMOKE TOO MUCH
GRASS, MAN.

2321
01:25:32,428 --> 01:25:33,496
I HOPE YOU DON'T THINK

2322
01:25:33,562 --> 01:25:36,299
YOU WALKIN' OFF NO PLACE
WITH ME, MAN.

2323
01:25:36,365 --> 01:25:38,601
MATTER OF FACT,
LET ME SIT OVER HERE.

2324
01:25:38,667 --> 01:25:39,502
DON'T FIGHT IT.

2325
01:25:42,104 --> 01:25:43,639
I'M NOT HERE WITH HIM.

2326
01:25:43,706 --> 01:25:46,108
I CAME BY MYSELF.
I'M A SOLO ARTIST.

2327
01:25:46,175 --> 01:25:47,710
[CLEARS THROAT]
I'M DOIN' MY OWN THING.

2328
01:25:49,578 --> 01:25:50,779
SECURITY.

2329
01:25:50,846 --> 01:25:52,481
DJ: A'IGHT, WE GOT
A NEW JOINT FOR Y'ALL.

2330
01:25:52,548 --> 01:25:53,816
I WANT YOU
TO CHECK THIS OUT.

2331
01:25:53,882 --> 01:25:56,219
NEW MILLENNIUM RECORDING
ARTISTS REN AND TEN.

2332
01:25:56,285 --> 01:25:57,253
Ten, rapping:
* HEY, YO, REN *

2333
01:25:57,320 --> 01:25:58,654
Ren: * YO,
WHAT'S UP, TEN? *

2334
01:25:58,721 --> 01:26:00,989
* BIG C TOLD ME
YOU WAS AT THE CLUB *

2335
01:26:01,056 --> 01:26:02,891
* PUSHIN' UP ON
ONE OF MY HOS *

2336
01:26:02,958 --> 01:26:04,327
* YO, YO, YO,
YOLANDA? *

2337
01:26:04,393 --> 01:26:05,361
* YEAH, YOLANDA *

2338
01:26:05,428 --> 01:26:06,529
* MAN, THAT HO
IS A HO *

2339
01:26:06,595 --> 01:26:08,431
* YOU STILL MESS
WITH THAT? *

2340
01:26:08,497 --> 01:26:11,367
* SHE MAY BE A HO,
BUT SHE'S MY HO, YOU KNOW? *

2341
01:26:11,434 --> 01:26:15,070
[SINGING]
* THE HO IS MINE *

2342
01:26:15,137 --> 01:26:17,172
* YOU GOTTA GET
THAT BITCH *

2343
01:26:17,240 --> 01:26:19,275
* THAT HO IS MINE... *

2344
01:26:19,342 --> 01:26:21,877
TRISH WILL SEE YOU NOW.

2345
01:26:21,944 --> 01:26:25,047
* I WAS FIRST IN LINE... *

2346
01:26:25,113 --> 01:26:27,583
WOW.

2347
01:26:27,650 --> 01:26:29,051
WOW.

2348
01:26:29,117 --> 01:26:32,988
Ten and Ren:
* MINE *

2349
01:26:33,055 --> 01:26:34,523
WOW.

2350
01:26:35,891 --> 01:26:37,092
Trish: BUT NOT BEFORE.

2351
01:26:37,159 --> 01:26:38,160
COME ON, NOW.

2352
01:26:38,227 --> 01:26:39,395
THANK YOU FOR YOUR TIME,
TRISH.

2353
01:26:39,462 --> 01:26:41,129
I'M FROM BROWN SUGAR
RECORDS.

2354
01:26:41,196 --> 01:26:42,565
AS YOU KNOW, I'M DRE--

2355
01:26:42,631 --> 01:26:44,066
PUT IT IN.

2356
01:26:44,132 --> 01:26:46,068
WE'LL KNOW ON THE 17th.

2357
01:26:46,134 --> 01:26:47,236
UH-HUH.

2358
01:26:47,303 --> 01:26:49,405
THURSDAY.

2359
01:26:50,806 --> 01:26:52,941
NOT AT 36, UH-UH.

2360
01:26:57,246 --> 01:26:58,547
YEAH.

2361
01:27:00,983 --> 01:27:02,618
UH-HUH.

2362
01:27:02,685 --> 01:27:03,886
THURSDAY.

2363
01:27:10,092 --> 01:27:11,360
MM-HMM.

2364
01:27:13,296 --> 01:27:15,531
YEAH. THE 3:00 SPOT.

2365
01:27:17,132 --> 01:27:18,601
[DRE'S CD PLAYS]

2366
01:27:18,667 --> 01:27:20,002
YEAH, HOLD THAT THOUGHT.
CAN YOU LEAVE ME

2367
01:27:20,068 --> 01:27:21,737
A COUPLE MORE OF THOSE?
AND THANKS FOR COMING BY.

2368
01:27:21,804 --> 01:27:22,771
GO AHEAD.

2369
01:27:22,838 --> 01:27:24,373
[CD PLAYING]

2370
01:27:24,440 --> 01:27:28,311
OK. THANK YOU
FOR COMING BY.

2371
01:27:28,377 --> 01:27:29,812
* I CAN FIX IT UP
RIGHT QUICK... *

2372
01:27:29,878 --> 01:27:31,314
Trish: HOW MANY?

2373
01:27:31,380 --> 01:27:32,381
[LAUGHING]

2374
01:27:32,448 --> 01:27:34,216
* LISTEN, Y'ALL... *

2375
01:27:34,283 --> 01:27:35,718
I DON'T THINK SO.

2376
01:27:37,586 --> 01:27:38,354
HEY.

2377
01:27:38,421 --> 01:27:40,022
WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?

2378
01:27:40,088 --> 01:27:42,791
I SAID TO GIVE ME SPACE AND
THEN YOU PULL THIS STUFF?

2379
01:27:42,858 --> 01:27:43,926
WHAT--

2380
01:27:43,992 --> 01:27:45,260
WHAT ARE YOU TALKIN' ABOUT?

2381
01:27:45,328 --> 01:27:46,495
GUESS WHAT DEMO I HEARD

2382
01:27:46,562 --> 01:27:48,997
FOR OUR UNSIGNED UNDERGROUND
REVIEW TODAY.

2383
01:27:49,064 --> 01:27:50,198
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

2384
01:27:50,265 --> 01:27:51,800
DRE, DON'T ACT LIKE
YOU DIDN'T PLAN THIS.

2385
01:27:51,867 --> 01:27:53,569
YOU KNOW THE EDITOR
DOES THE UNSIGNED REVIEWS.

2386
01:27:53,636 --> 01:27:55,270
WHY WOULD I NEED TO PLAN?

2387
01:27:55,338 --> 01:27:56,639
I COULD HAVE JUST
GIVEN IT TO YOU AT ANY TIME.

2388
01:27:56,705 --> 01:27:58,807
I WAS HOPING IT GOT
THE XXL

2389
01:27:58,874 --> 01:28:01,043
'CAUSE THE SHIT'S TIGHT,
NOT 'CAUSE I KNOW YOU.

2390
01:28:01,109 --> 01:28:02,511
WELL, I'M NOT DOING THE REVIEW.
I GAVE IT TO GABE.

2391
01:28:02,578 --> 01:28:03,679
WHY'D YOU GIVE IT
TO GABE?

2392
01:28:03,746 --> 01:28:05,714
I GAVE YOU MONEY
TO HELP START THE LABEL.

2393
01:28:05,781 --> 01:28:08,617
DOESN'T THE CONFLICT
OF INTEREST SEEM OBVIOUS?

2394
01:28:08,684 --> 01:28:10,085
[GROANS]

2395
01:28:10,152 --> 01:28:12,020
ALL RIGHT.
WELL, WHAT DID GABE SAY?

2396
01:28:12,087 --> 01:28:13,389
IT WASN'T A BAD REVIEW.

2397
01:28:13,456 --> 01:28:14,923
HE DISSED US.

2398
01:28:14,990 --> 01:28:17,426
HE DIDN'T DISS IT.
HE JUST WASN'T FEELIN' IT.

2399
01:28:17,493 --> 01:28:19,294
SID, YOU GOTTA STEP IN.
YOU GOTTA DO YOUR THING.

2400
01:28:19,362 --> 01:28:20,963
YOU'RE EDITOR. I MEAN,
YOU HEARD THE CD.

2401
01:28:21,029 --> 01:28:23,031
I CAN'T DO THAT, DRE.
I CAN'T STEP ON HIS REVIEW.

2402
01:28:23,098 --> 01:28:24,299
YOU'RE THE MAIN PERSON

2403
01:28:24,367 --> 01:28:25,634
THAT'S TALKIN' ABOUT
HIP-HOP LOSIN' ITS WAY,

2404
01:28:25,701 --> 01:28:28,303
HOW WE GOTTA GET BACK
TO ITS ROOTS.

2405
01:28:28,371 --> 01:28:29,738
WHAT'S WRONG WITH
GETTING IN TOUCH WITH WHY

2406
01:28:29,805 --> 01:28:31,374
WE BOTH FELL IN LOVE WITH
HIP-HOP IN THE FIRST PLACE?

2407
01:28:31,440 --> 01:28:33,409
'CAUSE IT'S ABOUT
FORWARD MOVEMENT.

2408
01:28:33,476 --> 01:28:34,877
INNOVATE AND MOVE ON.

2409
01:28:34,943 --> 01:28:37,312
ONE MINUTE YOU TALKIN' ABOUT
YOU WANT THINGS TO CHANGE,

2410
01:28:37,380 --> 01:28:38,547
AND THE NEXT MINUTE
YOU TALKING ABOUT

2411
01:28:38,614 --> 01:28:39,615
YOU WANT THINGS
TO STAY THE SAME.

2412
01:28:39,682 --> 01:28:41,750
I DO WANT THINGS
TO CHANGE.

2413
01:28:41,817 --> 01:28:43,619
I JUST DON'T LIKE
HOW THINGS HAVE CHANGED.

2414
01:28:43,686 --> 01:28:46,389
AND--AND I DIDN'T KNOW
THIS IS HOW IT WOULD TURN OUT.

2415
01:28:46,455 --> 01:28:48,190
AND THAT'S WHY WE NEED
TO LOOK BACK, OK?

2416
01:28:48,256 --> 01:28:49,658
'CAUSE IF WE LOOK BACK,

2417
01:28:49,725 --> 01:28:51,460
IT WILL MAKE US
SEE THINGS--

2418
01:28:51,527 --> 01:28:53,462
THE MISTAKES WE'VE MADE,

2419
01:28:53,529 --> 01:28:55,364
THINGS THAT WE NEVER KNEW
WERE THERE BEFORE.

2420
01:28:55,431 --> 01:28:57,500
AND IF WE JUST CAN STOP...

2421
01:28:59,267 --> 01:29:03,572
THEN MAYBE
WE CAN FIND THAT THING...

2422
01:29:03,639 --> 01:29:07,976
THAT WE BOTH KNOW
IS MISSING...

2423
01:29:08,043 --> 01:29:09,645
AND BUILD ON THAT.

2424
01:29:10,779 --> 01:29:12,548
ARE WE...

2425
01:29:12,615 --> 01:29:15,317
ARE WE STILL TALKING
ABOUT HIP-HOP?

2426
01:29:15,384 --> 01:29:17,686
THAT'S ALL
WE'VE EVER TALKED ABOUT.

2427
01:29:19,054 --> 01:29:21,189
IT'S ALL WE'VE EVER KNOWN...

2428
01:29:21,256 --> 01:29:23,492
FROM WHEN WE WERE 10.

2429
01:29:23,559 --> 01:29:26,161
SID, JUST DO ME A FAVOR.

2430
01:29:26,228 --> 01:29:30,365
BEFORE YOU DO SOMETHING
YOU MIGHT REGRET, JUST...

2431
01:29:30,433 --> 01:29:32,234
JUST LISTEN AGAIN.

2432
01:29:32,300 --> 01:29:35,070
JUST LISTEN AGAIN.

2433
01:29:35,137 --> 01:29:37,573
AND JUST FOLLOW
YOUR HEART.

2434
01:29:39,475 --> 01:29:42,545
AND WHATEVER YOU DECIDE...

2435
01:29:42,611 --> 01:29:45,581
WHATEVER YOU DECIDE
IS COOL.

2436
01:29:51,620 --> 01:29:53,922
WHATEVER YOU DECIDE
IS COOL.

2437
01:29:58,360 --> 01:29:59,294
DRE...

2438
01:29:59,361 --> 01:30:00,463
DRE.

2439
01:30:02,230 --> 01:30:03,832
I'VE MADE MY DECISION.

2440
01:30:09,905 --> 01:30:13,408
YOU AIN'T GONNA
CHANGE YOUR MIND?

2441
01:30:15,444 --> 01:30:18,046
WHAT ABOUT YOUR HEART, SID?

2442
01:30:18,113 --> 01:30:19,615
SID?

2443
01:30:28,824 --> 01:30:30,526
HEY.

2444
01:30:30,593 --> 01:30:32,961
CAN I GET YOU SOMETHING, SIR?

2445
01:30:33,028 --> 01:30:34,930
Reese: YES.

2446
01:30:34,997 --> 01:30:36,632
MACALLAN 25, NEAT.

2447
01:30:38,100 --> 01:30:39,201
HEY.

2448
01:30:39,267 --> 01:30:40,836
HEY.

2449
01:30:42,571 --> 01:30:44,473
YOU SMELL NICE.

2450
01:30:45,774 --> 01:30:47,075
UH...

2451
01:30:47,142 --> 01:30:48,511
YOU GONNA HAVE TO TREAT ME,

2452
01:30:48,577 --> 01:30:50,245
'CAUSE I CAN'T AFFORD
THAT SHIT NO MORE.

2453
01:30:50,312 --> 01:30:51,480
HERE.

2454
01:30:51,547 --> 01:30:53,882
PLEASE. YOU COULDN'T
AFFORD IT THEN, REMEMBER?

2455
01:30:53,949 --> 01:30:57,620
I HAD TO KEEP PLAYING
IF I WAS GONNA GET YOUR NUMBER.

2456
01:30:57,686 --> 01:31:02,991
DAMN. I LOST NEARLY
$200 THAT NIGHT.

2457
01:31:03,058 --> 01:31:04,993
YEAH, YEAH.

2458
01:31:10,499 --> 01:31:11,700
DRE...

2459
01:31:13,536 --> 01:31:15,571
[SIGHS]

2460
01:31:16,872 --> 01:31:19,274
SO, WHAT--
WHY'D YOU, UH...

2461
01:31:19,341 --> 01:31:21,109
WHY'D YOU CALL ME
HERE TONIGHT?

2462
01:31:21,176 --> 01:31:24,613
SO WE COULD HAVE A DRINK,
LAUGH ON OUR GOOD TIMES,

2463
01:31:24,680 --> 01:31:27,816
AND, UH, ACT LIKE
NONE OF THIS EVER HAPPENED?

2464
01:31:27,883 --> 01:31:29,552
YES AND NO.

2465
01:31:31,654 --> 01:31:34,790
I WENT TO
A DIVORCE LAWYER TODAY.

2466
01:31:34,857 --> 01:31:35,958
AND...

2467
01:31:36,024 --> 01:31:38,193
HE ASKED ME
ONE SIMPLE QUESTION.

2468
01:31:39,461 --> 01:31:41,964
HAVE WE TRIED
TO MAKE IT WORK?

2469
01:31:42,030 --> 01:31:44,132
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

2470
01:31:44,199 --> 01:31:46,001
DRE, LET ME FINISH.

2471
01:31:48,403 --> 01:31:50,372
WE NEVER TRIED.

2472
01:31:50,438 --> 01:31:52,440
WE JUST ASSUMED
IT WAS OVER,

2473
01:31:52,507 --> 01:31:54,309
LIKE WE WERE IN
HIGH SCHOOL OR SOMETHING.

2474
01:31:54,376 --> 01:31:56,178
BUT WE'RE NOT.
WE'RE MARRIED.

2475
01:31:58,581 --> 01:32:01,049
WE TOOK THOSE VOWS, DRE.

2476
01:32:05,120 --> 01:32:07,923
YOU BROKE THOSE VOWS.

2477
01:32:07,990 --> 01:32:09,091
COME ON.

2478
01:32:09,157 --> 01:32:12,094
I KNOW THAT YOU AND SIDNEY
HAVE SOMETHING VERY SPECIAL

2479
01:32:12,160 --> 01:32:14,029
THAT YOU SHARE.

2480
01:32:14,096 --> 01:32:17,933
I ALSO KNOW THERE'S A REASON
YOU MADE ME YOUR WIFE.

2481
01:32:18,000 --> 01:32:20,202
AND I...

2482
01:32:20,268 --> 01:32:22,170
AND I'M HOPING THAT
WHATEVER THAT REASON IS,

2483
01:32:22,237 --> 01:32:25,608
IT'S ENOUGH TO MAKE YOU WANT
TO KEEP ME AS YOUR WIFE.

2484
01:32:29,678 --> 01:32:31,213
OH, REESEY.

2485
01:32:36,885 --> 01:32:39,487
I DO.

2486
01:32:39,554 --> 01:32:41,123
I LOVE YOU.

2487
01:32:44,092 --> 01:32:48,797
BUT I THINK WE BOTH KNOW
THAT THIS CAN'T WORK.

2488
01:32:48,864 --> 01:32:52,300
I DON'T KNOW
IF WE HAVE ENOUGH OF...

2489
01:32:52,367 --> 01:32:55,137
WHAT IT TAKES TO...

2490
01:32:55,203 --> 01:32:56,504
TO MAKE THIS LAST.

2491
01:32:56,571 --> 01:33:00,308
I DON'T KNOW
IF WE EVER HAD ENOUGH.

2492
01:33:06,715 --> 01:33:09,017
WE CAN'T STAY MARRIED.

2493
01:33:10,185 --> 01:33:11,486
[FOOTSTEPS]

2494
01:33:11,553 --> 01:33:13,722
ANOTHER ROUND?

2495
01:33:21,296 --> 01:33:23,699
DAMN. WELL...

2496
01:33:23,766 --> 01:33:26,268
AT LEAST...

2497
01:33:26,334 --> 01:33:30,438
STAY A WHILE AND HAVE
A FEW DRINKS AND...

2498
01:33:30,505 --> 01:33:32,607
HAVE A FEW LAUGHS.

2499
01:33:39,782 --> 01:33:41,183
I HOPE YOU REALIZE
THIS MEANS

2500
01:33:41,249 --> 01:33:44,352
THAT I HAVE TO TAKE HALF
OF EVERYTHING YOU HAVE.

2501
01:33:44,419 --> 01:33:48,090
LET ME MAKE IT EASY ON YOU.

2502
01:33:49,291 --> 01:33:53,361
HERE'S MY LITTLE $58.25 NOW.

2503
01:34:12,547 --> 01:34:14,549
KELBY...

2504
01:34:14,616 --> 01:34:16,551
SORRY I'M LATE.
I'M SORRY.

2505
01:34:16,618 --> 01:34:18,320
WELL,
WE MISSED THE SHOW.

2506
01:34:19,955 --> 01:34:21,890
I'M SORRY.
I JUST GOT CAUGHT

2507
01:34:21,957 --> 01:34:24,292
IN THE MIDDLE
OF THIS TUG-OF-WAR

2508
01:34:24,359 --> 01:34:27,362
BETWEEN DRE'S LABEL
AND XXL AND...

2509
01:34:27,429 --> 01:34:28,663
[SIGHS]

2510
01:34:28,731 --> 01:34:30,398
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO DO.

2511
01:34:30,465 --> 01:34:31,867
I FEEL SO HELPLESS.

2512
01:34:37,639 --> 01:34:40,475
KELBY, WE CAN SEE THE SHOW
ON SATURDAY.

2513
01:34:40,542 --> 01:34:41,877
YEP.

2514
01:34:45,981 --> 01:34:48,383
WILL YOU WAIT UP
A SECOND?

2515
01:34:52,855 --> 01:34:55,023
HOW LONG ARE YOU TWO
GONNA PLAY THIS GAME?

2516
01:34:55,090 --> 01:34:56,691
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

2517
01:34:56,759 --> 01:34:58,861
WHAT AM I TALKING ABOUT?

2518
01:35:02,898 --> 01:35:04,332
YOU DON'T WANT
TO GET MARRIED.

2519
01:35:12,407 --> 01:35:14,810
I LOVE YOU.

2520
01:35:18,513 --> 01:35:21,316
BUT NOT THE WAY
YOU LOVE HIM.

2521
01:35:29,825 --> 01:35:31,359
I'M SORRY.

2522
01:35:33,028 --> 01:35:35,430
I DON'T KNOW WHY
YOUR HEART DOESN'T DO

2523
01:35:35,497 --> 01:35:36,832
WHAT YOUR MIND TELLS IT.

2524
01:35:36,899 --> 01:35:39,001
YOU DON'T KNOW.

2525
01:35:48,443 --> 01:35:50,378
I'M SORRY.

2526
01:36:02,891 --> 01:36:05,327
* LYING HERE *

2527
01:36:05,393 --> 01:36:07,896
* HOW BAD I FEEL *

2528
01:36:07,963 --> 01:36:11,533
* THE CLOCK TICK *

2529
01:36:11,599 --> 01:36:13,802
* AND I THINK OF YOU... *

2530
01:36:13,869 --> 01:36:16,404
Sidney: I ALWAYS THOUGHT,

2531
01:36:16,471 --> 01:36:19,107
ONE DAY I WOULD OUTGROW

2532
01:36:19,174 --> 01:36:21,276
MY RELATIONSHIP WITH HIP-HOP.

2533
01:36:21,343 --> 01:36:24,412
* CONFUSION *

2534
01:36:24,479 --> 01:36:25,981
* IS NOTHING NEW *

2535
01:36:26,048 --> 01:36:28,283
Sidney: I NEVER THOUGHT
IT WAS A FAD, LIKE MANY.

2536
01:36:28,350 --> 01:36:30,819
* FLASH BACK *

2537
01:36:30,886 --> 01:36:33,088
* ALL NIGHT *

2538
01:36:33,155 --> 01:36:35,690
BUT I NEVER THOUGHT
IT COULD GROW AND MATURE.

2539
01:36:35,757 --> 01:36:38,526
* ALMOST LEFT BEHIND *

2540
01:36:39,694 --> 01:36:43,298
* SUITCASE *

2541
01:36:43,365 --> 01:36:46,869
* OF MEMORIES *

2542
01:36:46,935 --> 01:36:52,340
* TIME AFTER SOMETIMES *

2543
01:36:52,407 --> 01:36:55,310
* YOU PICTURE ME *

2544
01:36:55,377 --> 01:36:57,679
* I'M WALKING *

2545
01:36:57,745 --> 01:37:01,616
* TOO FAR AHEAD *

2546
01:37:01,683 --> 01:37:06,188
* YOU'RE CALLING TO ME... *

2547
01:37:06,254 --> 01:37:09,257
Sidney: I THOUGHT IT WOULD BE
AN ADOLESCENT MEMORY

2548
01:37:09,324 --> 01:37:10,458
I'D LOOK BACK ON,

2549
01:37:10,525 --> 01:37:13,929
LIKE A CRUSH ON THE CAPTAIN
OF THE FOOTBALL TEAM.

2550
01:37:13,996 --> 01:37:16,564
BUT I REALIZE
WE HAVE MORE THAN THAT.

2551
01:37:16,631 --> 01:37:18,600
MUCH MORE.

2552
01:37:18,666 --> 01:37:20,869
WE HAVE A HISTORY...

2553
01:37:20,936 --> 01:37:22,871
A FRIENDSHIP.

2554
01:37:22,938 --> 01:37:25,307
WE LISTEN TO EACH OTHER.

2555
01:37:25,373 --> 01:37:27,242
WE LAUGH TOGETHER.

2556
01:37:27,309 --> 01:37:30,345
WE FINISH
EACH OTHER'S LYRICS.

2557
01:37:30,412 --> 01:37:33,515
I DON'T HAVE TO PRETEND
WITH HIP-HOP,

2558
01:37:33,581 --> 01:37:36,018
AND HIP-HOP DOESN'T
HAVE TO PRETEND WITH ME.

2559
01:37:36,084 --> 01:37:39,754
* YOU WILL FIND ME *

2560
01:37:39,821 --> 01:37:43,959
* TIME AFTER TIME *

2561
01:37:44,026 --> 01:37:47,629
Sidney: MY FEELINGS
HAVE NEVER BEEN MORE CLEAR,

2562
01:37:47,695 --> 01:37:49,031
AND I KNOW
THEY WILL NEVER GO AWAY.

2563
01:37:49,097 --> 01:37:51,433
* I'LL BE WAITING *

2564
01:37:51,499 --> 01:37:52,634
TO HIP-HOP.

2565
01:37:52,700 --> 01:37:56,638
* TIME AFTER TIME *

2566
01:37:56,704 --> 01:38:00,342
* MMM MMM... *

2567
01:38:07,715 --> 01:38:08,883
WAIT. DIDN'T I
ALREADY SEE YOU?

2568
01:38:08,951 --> 01:38:10,252
MM, YEAH.

2569
01:38:10,318 --> 01:38:12,120
SO WHAT ARE YOU DOING
BACK HERE?

2570
01:38:12,187 --> 01:38:14,789
I KNOW THAT Y'ALL
PUT A NEW SONG IN ROTATION

2571
01:38:14,856 --> 01:38:15,991
EVERY WEEK.

2572
01:38:16,058 --> 01:38:18,193
SO I FIGURE

2573
01:38:18,260 --> 01:38:21,229
I'M GONNA SHOW UP
EVERY WEEK

2574
01:38:21,296 --> 01:38:24,032
TILL YOU TAKE
A SERIOUS LISTEN TO THIS CD.

2575
01:38:24,099 --> 01:38:26,334
THEN I'M GONNA COME BACK

2576
01:38:26,401 --> 01:38:27,835
EVERY WEEK

2577
01:38:27,902 --> 01:38:31,039
UNTIL YOU PUT
THIS HERE CD INTO ROTATION.

2578
01:38:34,876 --> 01:38:37,445
EVERY WEEK.

2579
01:38:50,925 --> 01:38:53,228
SHE SAY NO.

2580
01:38:56,631 --> 01:38:58,033
YOU PLAYIN'.

2581
01:38:58,100 --> 01:38:59,634
UH-UH. NO, MAN.

2582
01:38:59,701 --> 01:39:00,635
YOU'RE NOT PLAYIN'?

2583
01:39:00,702 --> 01:39:01,903
I'M NOT PLAYIN', MAN.

2584
01:39:01,970 --> 01:39:03,371
YOU FOR REAL?

2585
01:39:03,438 --> 01:39:04,672
FOR REAL, MAN.

2586
01:39:04,739 --> 01:39:05,740
COME HERE, BOY!

2587
01:39:05,807 --> 01:39:06,741
YEAH!

2588
01:39:06,808 --> 01:39:07,809
YEAH, MAN.

2589
01:39:07,875 --> 01:39:09,644
IT'S YOU, MAN.
WHOO!

2590
01:39:09,711 --> 01:39:10,912
WHOO-HOO-HOO!

2591
01:39:10,979 --> 01:39:12,580
WE DID IT, MAN.

2592
01:39:12,647 --> 01:39:14,482
YOU ARE THE MAN!

2593
01:39:14,549 --> 01:39:16,518
* I WORSHIP AT THE TEMPLE
OF HIP-HOP *

2594
01:39:16,584 --> 01:39:18,420
* ATTENDED SERVICE,
ERIC GAVE A SERMON *

2595
01:39:18,486 --> 01:39:19,921
* BUT THE MINISTER
BECAME INTENSELY NERVOUS *

2596
01:39:19,988 --> 01:39:21,056
* WHEN THE KILLA PRIEST
WENT BUCK WILD *

2597
01:39:21,123 --> 01:39:22,157
* AND MADE THE REVEREND RUN *

2598
01:39:22,224 --> 01:39:23,191
* I REACHED IN... *

2599
01:39:23,258 --> 01:39:24,526
SHE SAID THE ANGIE
SHOW, RIGHT?

2600
01:39:31,133 --> 01:39:33,468
THEY STILL COME ON
AT THE SAME TIME, RIGHT?

2601
01:39:33,535 --> 01:39:35,337
YES, MAN.

2602
01:39:39,374 --> 01:39:42,177
STILL THINKING ABOUT
SIDNEY, HUH?

2603
01:39:45,013 --> 01:39:46,348
YEAH, MAN.

2604
01:39:46,414 --> 01:39:48,583
I TOLD YOU
YOU WAS A PUNK.

2605
01:39:49,817 --> 01:39:52,887
WHO YOU CALLIN' PUNK?

2606
01:39:52,954 --> 01:39:53,921
I KNOW
YOU BE TRIPPIN'.

2607
01:39:53,988 --> 01:39:55,223
GET YOUR BLACK ASS--

2608
01:39:55,290 --> 01:39:56,391
NOW, LET ME TELL YOU--

2609
01:39:56,458 --> 01:39:57,859
YOU BETTER SWITCH
TO THAT OLD CRACK,

